export const LUKE_OVERRIDES: Readonly<Record<string, string>> = {
  "1:1": "Since many have undertaken to set forth in order an account of the things that have been accomplished among us,",
  "1:2": "Just as they handed them down to us, who from the beginning were eyewitnesses and ministers of the word,",
  "1:3": "It seemed good to me also, having carefully followed all things from the beginning, to write to you in order, most excellent Theophilus,",
  "1:4": "So that you may know the truth of the words in which you have been instructed.",
  "1:6": "And they were both just before God, walking in all the commandments and ordinances of the Lord without blame.",
  "1:7": "And they had no son, because Elizabeth was barren: and they were both well advanced in years.",
  "1:8": "And it happened, while he was carrying out the priestly duty in the order of his course before God,",
  "1:9": "According to the custom of the priestly office, it fell to him by lot to offer incense, going into the temple of the Lord.",
  "1:10": "And all the crowd of the people was praying outside, at the hour of incense.",
  "1:12": "And Zachary, seeing him, was troubled: and fear fell upon him.",
  "1:14": "And you shall have joy and gladness: and many shall rejoice at his birth.",
  "1:17": "And he shall go before him in the spirit and power of Elias, to turn the hearts of the fathers to the children and the unbelieving to the wisdom of the just, to prepare for the Lord a perfect people.",
  "1:18": "And Zachary said to the angel: How shall I know this? For I am an old man, and my wife is advanced in years.",
  "1:19": "And the angel answered and said to him: I am Gabriel, who stand before God, and I am sent to speak to you and to bring you this good news.",
  "1:20": "And behold, you shall be unable to speak until the day when these things happen, because you have not believed my words, which shall be fulfilled in their time.",
  "1:21": "And the people were waiting for Zachary: and they wondered that he stayed so long in the temple.",
  "1:22": "And when he came out, he could not speak to them: and they understood that he had seen a vision in the temple. And he kept making signs to them and remained unable to speak.",
  "1:23": "And it happened, when the days of his service were completed, he went to his own house.",
  "1:25": "Thus has the Lord dealt with me in the days when he looked on me to take away my reproach among men.",
  "1:27": "To a virgin betrothed to a man whose name was Joseph, of the house of David: and the virgin's name was Mary.",
  "1:29": "And when she heard this, she was troubled at his saying and wondered within herself what kind of greeting this could be.",
  "1:34": "And Mary said to the angel: How shall this be done, because I know not man?",
  "1:35": "And the angel answered and said to her: The Holy Spirit shall come upon you and the power of the Most High shall overshadow you. And therefore also the Holy One who shall be born of you shall be called the Son of God.",
  "1:36": "And behold your cousin Elizabeth, she also has conceived a son in her old age: and this is the sixth month with her who is called barren.",
  "1:39": "And Mary, rising up in those days, went into the hill country with haste, into a city of Juda.",
  "1:40": "And she entered the house of Zachary and greeted Elizabeth.",
  "1:41": "And it happened that when Elizabeth heard the greeting of Mary, the infant leaped in her womb. And Elizabeth was filled with the Holy Spirit.",
  "1:44": "For behold, as soon as the voice of your greeting sounded in my ears, the infant in my womb leaped for joy.",
  "1:45": "And blessed are you who have believed, because those things shall be accomplished that were spoken to you by the Lord.",
  "1:49": "Because he who is mighty has done great things for me: and holy is his name.",
  "1:50": "And his mercy is from generation to generations, to those who fear him.",
  "1:51": "He has shown might in his arm: he has scattered the proud in the conceit of their heart.",
  "1:56": "And Mary stayed with her about three months. And she returned to her own house.",
  "1:57": "Now Elizabeth's full time to be delivered had come: and she brought forth a son.",
  "1:58": "And her neighbors and relatives heard that the Lord had shown his great mercy toward her: and they rejoiced with her.",
  "1:60": "And his mother answered and said: Not so. But he shall be called John.",
  "1:61": "And they said to her: There is no one among your relatives who is called by this name.",
  "1:62": "And they made signs to his father, asking what he would have him called.",
  "1:63": "And asking for a writing tablet, he wrote, saying: John is his name. And they all wondered.",
  "1:64": "And immediately his mouth was opened and his tongue freed: and he spoke, blessing God.",
  "1:65": "And fear came upon all their neighbors: and all these things were talked about through all the hill country of Judea.",
  "1:66": "And all who heard them kept them in their heart, saying: What kind of child, do you think, shall this be? For the hand of the Lord was with him.",
  "1:67": "And Zachary his father was filled with the Holy Spirit. And he prophesied, saying:",
  "1:68": "Blessed be the Lord God of Israel: because he has visited and brought about the redemption of his people.",
  "1:69": "And has raised up a horn of salvation for us, in the house of David his servant.",
  "1:70": "As he spoke by the mouth of his holy prophets, who have been from the beginning:",
  "1:71": "Salvation from our enemies and from the hand of all who hate us:",
  "1:72": "To show mercy to our fathers and to remember his holy covenant:",
  "1:73": "The oath which he swore to Abraham our father, that he would grant to us,",
  "1:76": "And you, child, shall be called the prophet of the Highest: for you shall go before the face of the Lord to prepare his ways:",
  "1:78": "Through the tender mercy of our God, in which the Dawn from on high has visited us:",
  "1:79": "To give light to those who sit in darkness and in the shadow of death: to guide our feet into the way of peace.",
  "1:80": "And the child grew and was strengthened in spirit: and was in the deserts until the day of his showing to Israel.",
  "2:2": "This first enrollment was made by Cyrinus, the governor of Syria.",
  "2:3": "And all went to be enrolled, each one to his own city.",
  "2:5": "To be enrolled with Mary his betrothed wife, who was with child.",
  "2:6": "And it happened that while they were there, her days were completed that she should be delivered.",
  "2:7": "And she brought forth her firstborn son and wrapped him up in swaddling clothes and laid him in a manger: because there was no room for them in the inn.",
  "2:8": "And there were in the same country shepherds living in the fields and keeping the night watches over their flock.",
  "2:9": "And behold an angel of the Lord stood by them and the brightness of God shone round about them: and they were very much afraid.",
  "2:10": "And the angel said to them: Fear not; for, behold, I bring you good news of great joy that shall be to all the people:",
  "2:13": "And suddenly there was with the angel a multitude of the heavenly army, praising God and saying:",
  "2:15": "And it happened, after the angels went away from them into heaven, the shepherds said to one another: Let us go over to Bethlehem and see this word that has happened, which the Lord has shown to us.",
  "2:17": "And seeing, they understood the word that had been spoken to them about this child.",
  "2:18": "And all who heard wondered at the things that were told them by the shepherds.",
  "2:20": "And the shepherds returned, glorifying and praising God for all the things they had heard and seen, just as it was told to them.",
  "2:21": "And after eight days were completed, when the child should be circumcised, his name was called JESUS, the name given by the angel before he was conceived in the womb.",
  "2:22": "And after the days of her purification, according to the law of Moses, were completed, they carried him to Jerusalem, to present him to the Lord:",
  "2:24": "And to offer a sacrifice, as it is written in the law of the Lord, a pair of turtledoves or two young pigeons.",
  "2:26": "And it had been revealed to him by the Holy Spirit that he should not see death before he had seen the Christ of the Lord.",
  "2:29": "Now you dismiss your servant, O Lord, according to your word in peace:",
  "2:31": "Which you have prepared before the face of all peoples:",
  "2:32": "A light for the revelation of the Gentiles and the glory of your people Israel.",
  "2:33": "And his father and mother were wondering at the things that were spoken about him.",
  "2:34": "And Simeon blessed them and said to Mary his mother: Behold, this child is set for the fall and for the resurrection of many in Israel and for a sign which shall be contradicted.",
  "2:35": "And your own soul a sword shall pierce, so that out of many hearts thoughts may be revealed.",
  "2:37": "And she was a widow until eighty-four years of age: she did not leave the temple, serving night and day with fasting and prayer.",
  "2:38": "Now she, coming in at that same hour, gave praise to the Lord: and spoke of him to all who were looking for the redemption of Israel.",
  "2:39": "And after they had done all things according to the law of the Lord, they returned into Galilee, to their city Nazareth.",
  "2:40": "And the child grew and became strong, full of wisdom: and the grace of God was in him.",
  "2:41": "And his parents went every year to Jerusalem, on the solemn day of the pasch.",
  "2:42": "And when he was twelve years old, they went up to Jerusalem, according to the custom of the feast.",
  "2:43": "And when they had completed the days and were returning, the child Jesus remained in Jerusalem. And his parents did not know it.",
  "2:44": "And thinking that he was in the company, they went a day's journey and looked for him among their relatives and friends.",
  "2:45": "And not finding him, they returned to Jerusalem, looking for him.",
  "2:46": "And it happened that after three days they found him in the temple, sitting in the midst of the teachers, listening to them and asking them questions.",
  "2:47": "And all who heard him were astonished at his wisdom and his answers.",
  "2:48": "And seeing him, they wondered. And his mother said to him: Son, why have you done so to us? Behold, your father and I have been looking for you in sorrow.",
  "2:49": "And he said to them: Why were you looking for me? Did you not know that I must be about my Father's business?",
  "2:50": "And they did not understand the word that he spoke to them.",
  "2:52": "And Jesus grew in wisdom and age and grace with God and men.",
  "3:2": "Under the high priests Anna and Caiphas, the word of the Lord came to John, the son of Zachary, in the desert.",
  "3:3": "And he came into all the country around the Jordan, preaching the baptism of penance for the forgiveness of sins.",
  "3:4": "As it is written in the book of the sayings of Isaiah the prophet: A voice of one crying in the wilderness: Prepare the way of the Lord, make straight his paths.",
  "3:7": "He said therefore to the crowds that came out to be baptized by him: You brood of vipers, who has warned you to flee from the wrath to come?",
  "3:8": "Bring forth therefore fruits worthy of penance: and do not begin to say, We have Abraham for our father. For I say to you that God is able from these stones to raise up children to Abraham.",
  "3:9": "For even now the axe is laid to the root of the trees. Every tree therefore that does not bring forth good fruit shall be cut down and cast into the fire.",
  "3:11": "And he answered and said to them: Whoever has two coats, let him give to the one who has none; and whoever has food, let him do the same.",
  "3:13": "But he said to them: Do nothing more than what is appointed for you.",
  "3:14": "And the soldiers also asked him, saying: And what shall we do? And he said to them: Do violence to no one, do not falsely accuse anyone; and be content with your pay.",
  "3:15": "And as the people were wondering, and all were thinking in their hearts about John, whether perhaps he might be the Christ,",
  "3:16": "John answered, saying to all: I indeed baptize you with water: but one mightier than I is coming, the strap of whose sandals I am not worthy to untie. He shall baptize you with the Holy Spirit and with fire.",
  "3:17": "His winnowing fan is in his hand: and he will clean his threshing floor and will gather the wheat into his barn: but the chaff he will burn with unquenchable fire.",
  "3:18": "And with many other exhortations he preached to the people.",
  "3:20": "He added this also to them all, that he shut up John in prison.",
  "3:21": "Now it happened, when all the people were being baptized, that Jesus also was baptized; and as he was praying, heaven was opened.",
  "3:22": "And the Holy Spirit descended in bodily form, like a dove, upon him. And a voice came from heaven: You are my beloved Son. In you I am well pleased.",
  "3:23": "And Jesus himself was beginning to be about thirty years of age: being (as was supposed) the son of Joseph, who was of Heli, who was of Mathat,",
  "3:36": "Who was of Cainan, who was of Arphaxad, who was of Sem, who was of Noe, who was of Lamech,",
  "4:1": "And Jesus, full of the Holy Spirit, returned from the Jordan and was led by the Spirit into the desert",
  "4:2": "For forty days, and was tempted by the devil. And he ate nothing in those days. And when they were ended, he was hungry.",
  "4:6": "And he said to him: To you I will give all this power and the glory of them. For they have been handed over to me: and to whomever I will, I give them.",
  "4:7": "If you therefore will adore before me, all shall be yours.",
  "4:8": "And Jesus answered and said to him: It is written: You shall adore the Lord your God, and him only shall you serve.",
  "4:9": "And he brought him to Jerusalem and set him on a pinnacle of the temple and said to him: If you are the Son of God, cast yourself down from here.",
  "4:10": "For it is written that He has given his angels charge over you, that they keep you,",
  "4:11": "And that in their hands they shall bear you up, so that you do not dash your foot against a stone.",
  "4:12": "And Jesus answered and said to him: It is said: You shall not tempt the Lord your God.",
  "4:13": "And when all the temptation was ended, the devil departed from him for a time.",
  "4:14": "And Jesus returned in the power of the Spirit into Galilee: and news of him went out through the whole country.",
  "4:15": "And he taught in their synagogues and was praised by all.",
  "4:17": "And the book of Isaiah the prophet was handed to him. And as he unrolled the book, he found the place where it was written:",
  "4:18": "The Spirit of the Lord is upon me. Therefore he has anointed me to preach the gospel to the poor, he has sent me to heal the contrite of heart,",
  "4:19": "To preach deliverance to the captives and sight to the blind, to set at liberty those who are bruised, to preach the acceptable year of the Lord and the day of reward.",
  "4:20": "And when he had rolled up the book, he gave it back to the attendant and sat down. And the eyes of all in the synagogue were fixed on him.",
  "4:21": "And he began to say to them: Today this scripture is fulfilled in your hearing.",
  "4:22": "And all spoke well of him. And they wondered at the words of grace that came from his mouth. And they said: Is not this the son of Joseph?",
  "4:23": "And he said to them: Surely you will say to me this proverb: Physician, heal yourself. The great things we have heard were done in Capernaum, do also here in your own country.",
  "4:25": "In truth I say to you, there were many widows in Israel in the days of Elias, when heaven was shut up three years and six months, when there was a great famine throughout all the land.",
  "4:26": "And to none of them was Elias sent, but to Sarepta of Sidon, to a widow.",
  "4:28": "And all those in the synagogue, hearing these things, were filled with anger.",
  "4:29": "And they rose up and drove him out of the city: and they brought him to the brow of the hill on which their city was built, so that they might throw him down headlong.",
  "4:30": "But he, passing through the midst of them, went his way.",
  "4:32": "And they were astonished at his teaching: for his word was with power.",
  "4:34": "Saying: Leave us alone. What have we to do with you, Jesus of Nazareth? Have you come to destroy us? I know who you are, the Holy One of God.",
  "4:35": "And Jesus rebuked him, saying: Be quiet and come out of him. And when the devil had thrown him down in their midst, he went out of him and did him no harm at all.",
  "4:36": "And fear came upon all; and they talked among themselves, saying: What word is this? For with authority and power he commands the unclean spirits, and they go out.",
  "4:37": "And news of him spread into every place in the country.",
  "4:38": "And Jesus, rising up out of the synagogue, went into Simon's house. And Simon's mother-in-law was sick with a great fever: and they begged him for her.",
  "4:39": "And standing over her, he commanded the fever: and it left her. And immediately rising, she served them.",
  "4:40": "And when the sun had set, all who had any sick with various diseases brought them to him. But he, laying his hands on every one of them, healed them.",
  "4:41": "And devils went out from many, crying out and saying: You are the Son of God. And rebuking them, he did not allow them to speak; for they knew that he was the Christ.",
  "4:42": "And when it was day, going out, he went into a desert place: and the crowds looked for him and came to him. And they tried to keep him from leaving them.",
  "4:43": "And he said to them: I must preach the kingdom of God to other cities also: for this is why I am sent.",
  "5:1": "And it happened that when the crowds pressed upon him to hear the word of God, he stood by the lake of Genesareth,",
  "5:2": "And saw two boats standing by the lake: but the fishermen had gone out of them and were washing their nets.",
  "5:3": "And getting into one of the boats, which was Simon's, he asked him to put out a little from the land. And sitting down, he taught the crowds from the boat.",
  "5:4": "Now when he had stopped speaking, he said to Simon: Put out into the deep and let down your nets for a catch.",
  "5:5": "And Simon answered and said to him: Master, we have worked all night and have caught nothing: but at your word I will let down the net.",
  "5:6": "And when they had done this, they enclosed a very great number of fish: and their net was breaking.",
  "5:7": "And they signaled to their partners who were in the other boat to come and help them. And they came and filled both the boats, so that they were almost sinking.",
  "5:8": "When Simon Peter saw this, he fell down at Jesus' knees, saying: Depart from me, for I am a sinful man, O Lord.",
  "5:9": "For he was completely astonished, and all who were with him, at the catch of fish which they had taken.",
  "5:10": "And so also were James and John, the sons of Zebedee, who were Simon's partners. And Jesus said to Simon: Fear not: from now on you shall catch men.",
  "5:11": "And having brought their boats to land, leaving all things, they followed him.",
  "5:12": "And it happened, when he was in a certain city, behold a man full of leprosy who, seeing Jesus and falling on his face, begged him, saying: Lord, if you will, you can make me clean.",
  "5:13": "And stretching out his hand, he touched him, saying: I will. Be cleansed. And immediately the leprosy left him.",
  "5:14": "And he ordered him to tell no one, but: Go, show yourself to the priest and offer for your cleansing as Moses commanded, for a testimony to them.",
  "5:15": "But news of him spread all the more: and great crowds came together to hear and to be healed by him of their sicknesses.",
  "5:16": "And he withdrew into the desert and prayed.",
  "5:17": "And it happened on a certain day, as he sat teaching, that there were also Pharisees and teachers of the law sitting by, who had come out of every town of Galilee and Judea and Jerusalem: and the power of the Lord was present to heal them.",
  "5:18": "And behold, men were carrying on a bed a man who was paralyzed: and they were trying to bring him in and lay him before him.",
  "5:19": "And when they could not find a way to bring him in, because of the crowd, they went up onto the roof and let him down through the tiles with his bed into the midst before Jesus.",
  "5:20": "When he saw their faith, he said: Man, your sins are forgiven you.",
  "5:22": "And when Jesus knew their thoughts, he answered and said to them: What are you thinking in your hearts?",
  "5:24": "But so that you may know that the Son of man has power on earth to forgive sins (he said to the paralyzed man), I say to you: Arise, take up your bed and go into your house.",
  "5:26": "And all were astonished: and they glorified God. And they were filled with fear, saying: We have seen wonderful things today.",
  "5:27": "And after these things, he went out and saw a tax collector named Levi, sitting at the tax booth: and he said to him: Follow me.",
  "5:29": "And Levi made him a great feast in his own house: and there was a great company of tax collectors and of others who were at table with them.",
  "5:31": "And Jesus answered and said to them: Those who are well do not need the physician, but those who are sick.",
  "5:32": "I did not come to call the just, but sinners to penance.",
  "5:33": "And they said to him: Why do the disciples of John fast often and make prayers, and the disciples of the Pharisees likewise; but yours eat and drink?",
  "5:34": "And he said to them: Can you make the friends of the bridegroom fast while the bridegroom is with them?",
  "5:35": "But the days will come when the bridegroom shall be taken away from them: then they shall fast in those days.",
  "5:36": "And he also told them a parable: No one puts a piece from a new garment upon an old garment: otherwise he both tears the new, and the piece taken from the new does not match the old.",
  "5:37": "And no one puts new wine into old wineskins: otherwise the new wine will burst the wineskins; and it will be spilled and the wineskins will be ruined.",
  "5:38": "But new wine must be put into new wineskins: and both are preserved.",
  "5:39": "And no one, after drinking old wine, at once wants new: for he says: The old is better.",
  "6:1": "And it happened on the second first sabbath that, as he went through the grain fields, his disciples plucked the ears and ate them, rubbing them in their hands.",
  "6:2": "And some of the Pharisees said to them: Why do you do what is not lawful on the sabbath days?",
  "6:3": "And Jesus answered them and said: Have you not read even this, what David did when he was hungry, and those who were with him:",
  "6:4": "How he went into the house of God and took and ate the bread of proposition and gave it to those who were with him, which is not lawful to eat except for the priests alone?",
  "6:7": "And the scribes and Pharisees watched to see if he would heal on the sabbath, so that they might find a charge against him.",
  "6:8": "But he knew their thoughts and said to the man who had the withered hand: Arise and stand up in the midst. And rising, he stood up.",
  "6:9": "Then Jesus said to them: I ask you, is it lawful on the sabbath days to do good or to do evil? To save life or to destroy it?",
  "6:10": "And looking around at them all, he said to the man: Stretch out your hand. And he stretched it out. And his hand was restored.",
  "6:11": "And they were filled with fury: and they talked with one another about what they might do to Jesus.",
  "6:12": "And it happened in those days that he went out to a mountain to pray: and he spent the whole night in prayer to God.",
  "6:13": "And when day had come, he called his disciples to him: and he chose twelve of them (whom he also named apostles):",
  "6:14": "Simon, whom he named Peter, and Andrew his brother, James and John, Philip and Bartholomew,",
  "6:16": "And Jude the brother of James, and Judas Iscariot, who became the traitor.",
  "6:17": "And coming down with them, he stood on a level place: and with him the company of his disciples and a very great crowd of people from all Judea and Jerusalem and the sea coast, both of Tyre and Sidon,",
  "6:18": "Who had come to hear him and to be healed of their diseases. And those who were troubled with unclean spirits were cured.",
  "6:19": "And all the crowd tried to touch him: for power went out from him and healed all.",
  "6:21": "Blessed are you who hunger now: for you shall be filled. Blessed are you who weep now: for you shall laugh.",
  "6:22": "Blessed shall you be when men shall hate you, and when they shall separate you and shall insult you and cast out your name as evil, for the sake of the Son of man.",
  "6:23": "Be glad in that day and rejoice: for behold, your reward is great in heaven. For in the same way their fathers treated the prophets.",
  "6:24": "But woe to you who are rich: for you have your consolation.",
  "6:25": "Woe to you who are filled: for you shall hunger. Woe to you who laugh now: for you shall mourn and weep.",
  "6:26": "Woe to you when men shall speak well of you: for in the same way their fathers treated the false prophets.",
  "6:27": "But I say to you who hear: Love your enemies. Do good to those who hate you.",
  "6:28": "Bless those who curse you and pray for those who falsely accuse you.",
  "6:29": "And to him who strikes you on the one cheek, offer also the other. And from him who takes away your cloak, do not withhold your coat also.",
  "6:30": "Give to everyone who asks you: and from him who takes away your goods, do not ask for them back.",
  "6:31": "And as you would have men do to you, do also to them in the same way.",
  "6:32": "And if you love those who love you, what thanks do you deserve? For sinners also love those who love them.",
  "6:33": "And if you do good to those who do good to you, what thanks do you deserve? For sinners also do this.",
  "6:34": "And if you lend to those from whom you hope to receive, what thanks do you deserve? For sinners also lend to sinners, to receive as much in return.",
  "6:35": "But love your enemies: do good, and lend, hoping for nothing in return: and your reward shall be great, and you shall be the sons of the Highest. For he is kind to the ungrateful and to the evil.",
  "6:36": "Be therefore merciful, as your Father also is merciful.",
  "6:38": "Give: and it shall be given to you: good measure and pressed down and shaken together and running over shall they pour into your lap. For with the same measure that you measure out, it shall be measured to you again.",
  "6:39": "And he also told them a parable: Can the blind lead the blind? Will they not both fall into the ditch?",
  "6:40": "The disciple is not above his teacher: but everyone shall be perfect if he is like his teacher.",
  "6:41": "And why do you see the speck in your brother's eye, but do not notice the beam that is in your own eye?",
  "6:42": "Or how can you say to your brother: Brother, let me take the speck out of your eye, when you yourself do not see the beam in your own eye? Hypocrite, first take the beam out of your own eye: and then you shall see clearly to take the speck out of your brother's eye.",
  "6:44": "For every tree is known by its fruit. For men do not gather figs from thorns: nor do they gather grapes from a bramble bush.",
  "6:45": "A good man out of the good treasure of his heart brings forth what is good: and an evil man out of the evil treasure brings forth what is evil. For out of the abundance of the heart the mouth speaks.",
  "6:46": "And why do you call me Lord, Lord, and do not do the things which I say?",
  "6:47": "Everyone who comes to me and hears my words and does them, I will show you whom he is like.",
  "6:48": "He is like a man building a house, who dug deep and laid the foundation upon a rock. And when a flood came, the stream beat hard against that house: and it could not shake it: for it was founded on a rock.",
  "6:49": "But he who hears and does not do is like a man building his house upon the earth without a foundation: against which the stream beat hard. And immediately it fell: and the ruin of that house was great.",
  "7:2": "And the servant of a certain centurion, who was dear to him, was sick and about to die.",
  "7:3": "And when he heard of Jesus, he sent to him the ancients of the Jews, asking him to come and heal his servant.",
  "7:4": "And when they came to Jesus, they begged him earnestly, saying to him: He is worthy that you should do this for him.",
  "7:6": "And Jesus went with them. And when he was now not far from the house, the centurion sent his friends to him, saying: Lord, do not trouble yourself; for I am not worthy that you should enter under my roof.",
  "7:7": "That is why I did not think myself worthy to come to you: but say the word, and my servant shall be healed.",
  "7:9": "When Jesus heard this, he marveled: and turning to the crowd that followed him, he said: Amen I say to you, I have not found so great faith, not even in Israel.",
  "7:10": "And those who were sent, returning to the house, found the servant who had been sick in good health.",
  "7:11": "And it happened afterwards that he went into a city called Naim: and his disciples and a great crowd went with him.",
  "7:12": "And when he came near the gate of the city, behold a dead man was being carried out, the only son of his mother: and she was a widow. And a great crowd of the city was with her.",
  "7:13": "When the Lord saw her, being moved with mercy toward her, he said to her: Weep not.",
  "7:14": "And he came near and touched the bier. And those who carried it stood still. And he said: Young man, I say to you, arise.",
  "7:15": "And he who was dead sat up and began to speak. And he gave him to his mother.",
  "7:16": "And fear came upon them all: and they glorified God, saying: A great prophet has risen up among us: and, God has visited his people.",
  "7:17": "And this report about him went out throughout all Judea and throughout all the country round about.",
  "7:19": "And John called two of his disciples to him and sent them to Jesus, saying: Are you he who is to come? Or should we look for another?",
  "7:20": "And when the men had come to him, they said: John the Baptist has sent us to you, saying: Are you he who is to come? Or should we look for another?",
  "7:21": "(And in that same hour, he cured many of their diseases and afflictions and evil spirits: and to many who were blind he gave sight.)",
  "7:22": "And he answered and said to them: Go and tell John what you have heard and seen: the blind see, the lame walk, the lepers are made clean, the deaf hear, the dead rise again, to the poor the gospel is preached.",
  "7:23": "And blessed is he who shall not be scandalized in me.",
  "7:24": "And when the messengers of John had gone, he began to speak to the crowds about John. What did you go out into the desert to see? A reed shaken by the wind?",
  "7:25": "But what did you go out to see? A man clothed in soft garments? Behold, those who are in costly clothing and live in luxury are in the houses of kings.",
  "7:26": "But what did you go out to see? A prophet? Yes, I say to you, and more than a prophet.",
  "7:28": "For I say to you: Among those who are born of women, there is not a greater prophet than John the Baptist. But he who is the least in the kingdom of God is greater than he.",
  "7:29": "And all the people who heard, and the tax collectors, justified God, having been baptized with John's baptism.",
  "7:30": "But the Pharisees and the lawyers rejected the counsel of God against themselves, not having been baptized by him.",
  "7:31": "And the Lord said: To what then shall I compare the men of this generation? And what are they like?",
  "7:32": "They are like children sitting in the marketplace and calling to one another and saying: We have piped to you, and you have not danced: we have mourned, and you have not wept.",
  "7:34": "The Son of man has come eating and drinking. And you say: Behold a man who is a glutton and a drinker of wine, a friend of tax collectors and sinners.",
  "7:36": "And one of the Pharisees asked him to eat with him. And he went into the house of the Pharisee and sat down at table.",
  "7:37": "And behold a woman who was in the city, a sinner, when she knew that he was at table in the Pharisee's house, brought an alabaster box of ointment.",
  "7:38": "And standing behind at his feet, she began to wash his feet with tears and wiped them with the hair of her head and kissed his feet and anointed them with the ointment.",
  "7:39": "And the Pharisee who had invited him, seeing it, said within himself: This man, if he were a prophet, would surely know who and what kind of woman this is who touches him, that she is a sinner.",
  "7:40": "And Jesus answered and said to him: Simon, I have something to say to you. And he said: Master, say it.",
  "7:42": "And since they had nothing with which to pay, he forgave them both. Which of the two, therefore, loves him more?",
  "7:43": "Simon answered and said: I suppose the one to whom he forgave more. And he said to him: You have judged rightly.",
  "7:44": "And turning to the woman, he said to Simon: Do you see this woman? I entered your house: you gave me no water for my feet. But she has washed my feet with tears; and with her hair has wiped them.",
  "7:45": "You gave me no kiss. But she, since she came in, has not stopped kissing my feet.",
  "7:47": "Therefore I say to you: Many sins are forgiven her, because she has loved much. But to whom less is forgiven, he loves less.",
  "7:49": "And those who sat at table with him began to say within themselves: Who is this who even forgives sins?",
  "7:50": "And he said to the woman: Your faith has saved you. Go in peace.",
  "8:1": "And it happened afterwards that he traveled through the cities and towns, preaching and proclaiming the good news of the kingdom of God: and the twelve were with him,",
  "8:2": "And certain women who had been healed of evil spirits and sicknesses: Mary who is called Magdalene, out of whom seven devils had gone out,",
  "8:3": "And Joanna the wife of Chusa, Herod's steward, and Susanna and many others who provided for him out of their own means.",
  "8:4": "And when a very great crowd had gathered together and people were hurrying to him out of the cities, he spoke in a parable.",
  "8:5": "The sower went out to sow his seed. And as he sowed, some fell by the wayside. And it was trodden down: and the birds of the air ate it up.",
  "8:6": "And some other seed fell upon rock. And as soon as it had sprung up, it withered away, because it had no moisture.",
  "8:7": "And some other fell among thorns. And the thorns, growing up with it, choked it.",
  "8:8": "And some other fell upon good ground and, having sprung up, yielded fruit a hundredfold. Saying these things, he cried out: Whoever has ears to hear, let him hear.",
  "8:10": "And he said to them: To you it is given to know the mystery of the kingdom of God; but to the rest in parables, so that seeing they may not see and hearing they may not understand.",
  "8:12": "And those by the wayside are the ones who hear: then the devil comes and takes the word out of their heart, so that they may not believe and be saved.",
  "8:13": "Now those upon the rock are the ones who, when they hear, receive the word with joy: and these have no roots: for they believe for a while and in time of temptation they fall away.",
  "8:14": "And what fell among thorns are those who have heard and, going their way, are choked with the cares and riches and pleasures of this life and yield no fruit.",
  "8:15": "But what is on the good ground are those who, in a good and perfect heart, hearing the word, keep it and bring forth fruit in patience.",
  "8:16": "Now no one lighting a candle covers it with a vessel or puts it under a bed: but he sets it upon a candlestick, so that those who come in may see the light.",
  "8:17": "For there is nothing secret that shall not be made known, nor hidden that shall not be known and come out into the open.",
  "8:19": "And his mother and brethren came to him: and they could not get to him because of the crowd.",
  "8:20": "And it was told him: Your mother and your brethren are standing outside, wanting to see you.",
  "8:21": "And he answered and said to them: My mother and my brethren are those who hear the word of God and do it.",
  "8:22": "And it happened on a certain day that he got into a little boat with his disciples. And he said to them: Let us go over to the other side of the lake. And they set out.",
  "8:23": "And while they were sailing, he slept. And a windstorm came down upon the lake: and they were filling with water and were in danger.",
  "8:24": "And they came and woke him, saying: Master, we are perishing. But he, arising, rebuked the wind and the raging of the water. And it stopped: and there was a calm.",
  "8:25": "And he said to them: Where is your faith? And they, being afraid, wondered, saying to one another: Who do you think this is, that he commands both the winds and the sea: and they obey him?",
  "8:26": "And they sailed to the country of the Gerasenes, which is opposite Galilee.",
  "8:27": "And when he had come out onto the land, he was met by a certain man who had had a devil for a very long time. And he wore no clothes: and he did not live in a house, but in the tombs.",
  "8:28": "And when he saw Jesus, he fell down before him. And crying out with a loud voice, he said: What have I to do with you, Jesus, Son of the most high God? I beg you, do not torment me.",
  "8:29": "For he was commanding the unclean spirit to go out of the man. For many times it had seized him: and he was bound with chains and kept in fetters: and breaking the bonds, he was driven by the devil into the deserts.",
  "8:30": "And Jesus asked him, saying: What is your name? And he said: Legion. Because many devils had entered into him.",
  "8:31": "And they begged him not to command them to go into the abyss.",
  "8:32": "And there was a herd of many swine feeding there on the mountain: and they begged him to allow them to enter into them. And he allowed them.",
  "8:33": "The devils therefore went out of the man and entered the swine. And the herd rushed violently down a steep place into the lake and were drowned.",
  "8:34": "When those who fed them saw what was done, they fled and told it in the city and in the villages.",
  "8:35": "And they went out to see what had been done. And they came to Jesus and found the man from whom the devils had departed, sitting at his feet, clothed and in his right mind. And they were afraid.",
  "8:36": "And those who had seen it also told them how he had been healed from the legion.",
  "8:37": "And all the crowd of the country of the Gerasenes begged him to depart from them: for they were seized with great fear. And he, getting into the boat, went back again.",
  "8:38": "Now the man from whom the devils had departed begged him that he might be with him. But Jesus sent him away, saying:",
  "8:39": "Return to your house and tell what great things God has done for you. And he went through the whole city, proclaiming what great things Jesus had done for him.",
  "8:40": "And it happened that when Jesus had returned, the crowd welcomed him: for they were all waiting for him.",
  "8:41": "And behold, there came a man whose name was Jairus: and he was a ruler of the synagogue. And he fell down at the feet of Jesus, begging him to come into his house:",
  "8:42": "For he had an only daughter, about twelve years old, and she was dying. And it happened, as he went, that he was pressed in by the crowds.",
  "8:43": "And there was a certain woman who had had a flow of blood for twelve years, who had spent all she had on physicians and could not be healed by any.",
  "8:44": "She came behind him and touched the hem of his garment: and immediately the flow of her blood stopped.",
  "8:45": "And Jesus said: Who is it that touched me? And as all were denying it, Peter and those who were with him said: Master, the crowds press around you and push against you; and you say, Who touched me?",
  "8:46": "And Jesus said: Somebody has touched me; for I know that power has gone out from me.",
  "8:47": "And the woman, seeing that she was not hidden, came trembling and fell down before his feet and declared before all the people why she had touched him, and how she was immediately healed.",
  "8:49": "While he was still speaking, someone came to the ruler of the synagogue, saying to him: Your daughter is dead: do not trouble him.",
  "8:50": "And Jesus, hearing this word, answered the father of the girl: Fear not. Only believe: and she shall be saved.",
  "8:51": "And when he had come to the house, he did not allow anyone to go in with him, except Peter and James and John, and the father and mother of the girl.",
  "8:52": "And all were weeping and mourning for her. But he said: Weep not. The girl is not dead, but sleeping.",
  "8:53": "And they laughed at him, knowing that she was dead.",
  "8:54": "But he, taking her by the hand, cried out, saying: Girl, arise.",
  "8:55": "And her spirit returned: and she arose immediately. And he told them to give her something to eat.",
  "8:56": "And her parents were astonished, and he ordered them to tell no one what had been done.",
  "9:3": "And he said to them: Take nothing for your journey, neither staff, nor bag, nor bread, nor money; and do not have two coats.",
  "9:4": "And whatever house you enter, stay there and do not leave from there.",
  "9:6": "And going out, they went about through the towns, preaching the gospel and healing everywhere.",
  "9:7": "Now Herod the tetrarch heard of all the things that were done by him. And he was puzzled, because it was said",
  "9:8": "By some that John had risen from the dead: but by some others, that Elias had appeared: and by others, that one of the old prophets had risen again.",
  "9:9": "And Herod said: John I have beheaded. But who is this of whom I hear such things? And he tried to see him.",
  "9:10": "And the apostles, when they had returned, told him all they had done. And taking them, he went aside to a desert place, apart, which belongs to Bethsaida.",
  "9:11": "When the people knew it, they followed him: and he welcomed them and spoke to them of the kingdom of God and healed those who had need of healing.",
  "9:12": "Now the day began to wear away. And the twelve came and said to him: Send away the crowd, so that, going into the towns and villages round about, they may find lodging and get food; for we are here in a desert place.",
  "9:13": "But he said to them: You give them something to eat. And they said: We have no more than five loaves and two fish; unless perhaps we should go and buy food for all this crowd.",
  "9:14": "Now there were about five thousand men. And he said to his disciples: Make them sit down in groups of fifty.",
  "9:16": "And taking the five loaves and the two fish, he looked up to heaven and blessed them: and he broke them and gave them to his disciples to set before the crowd.",
  "9:17": "And they all ate and were filled. And of the fragments that remained, twelve baskets were taken up.",
  "9:18": "And it happened, as he was praying alone, that his disciples were also with him: and he asked them, saying: Who do the people say that I am?",
  "9:19": "But they answered and said: John the Baptist; but some say Elias: and others say that one of the former prophets has risen again.",
  "9:20": "And he said to them: But who do you say that I am? Simon Peter answered and said: The Christ of God.",
  "9:21": "But he strictly warned them and commanded them to tell this to no one,",
  "9:22": "Saying: The Son of man must suffer many things and be rejected by the ancients and chief priests and scribes and be killed and on the third day rise again.",
  "9:23": "And he said to all: If anyone will come after me, let him deny himself and take up his cross daily and follow me.",
  "9:24": "For whoever will save his life shall lose it: for whoever shall lose his life for my sake shall save it.",
  "9:25": "For what does it profit a man if he gains the whole world and loses himself and casts himself away?",
  "9:26": "For whoever shall be ashamed of me and of my words, of him the Son of man shall be ashamed, when he shall come in his majesty and that of his Father and of the holy angels.",
  "9:27": "But I tell you truly: There are some standing here who shall not taste death until they see the kingdom of God.",
  "9:28": "And it happened, about eight days after these words, that he took Peter and James and John and went up a mountain to pray.",
  "9:29": "And while he prayed, the appearance of his face was changed and his clothing became white and shining.",
  "9:30": "And behold, two men were talking with him. And they were Moses and Elias,",
  "9:31": "Appearing in majesty. And they spoke of his departure which he was to accomplish in Jerusalem.",
  "9:32": "But Peter and those who were with him were heavy with sleep. And waking, they saw his glory and the two men who stood with him.",
  "9:33": "And it happened that, as they were departing from him, Peter said to Jesus: Master, it is good for us to be here: and let us make three tabernacles, one for you, and one for Moses, and one for Elias: not knowing what he said.",
  "9:34": "And as he spoke these things, a cloud came and overshadowed them. And they were afraid when they entered the cloud.",
  "9:35": "And a voice came out of the cloud, saying: This is my beloved Son. Hear him.",
  "9:36": "And when the voice had spoken, Jesus was found alone. And they kept silent and told no one in those days any of the things which they had seen.",
  "9:37": "And it happened on the following day, when they came down from the mountain, that a great crowd met him.",
  "9:38": "And behold, a man in the crowd cried out, saying: Master, I beg you, look upon my son, because he is my only one.",
  "9:39": "And behold, a spirit seizes him, and he suddenly cries out, and it throws him down and tears him, so that he foams; and bruising him, it hardly leaves him.",
  "9:40": "And I asked your disciples to cast him out: and they could not.",
  "9:41": "And Jesus answered and said: O faithless and perverse generation, how long shall I be with you and bear with you? Bring your son here.",
  "9:44": "And all were astonished at the mighty power of God. But while all were wondering at all the things he did, he said to his disciples: Lay up these words in your hearts, for the Son of man shall be delivered into the hands of men.",
  "9:45": "But they did not understand this word: and it was hidden from them, so that they did not grasp it. And they were afraid to ask him about this word.",
  "9:46": "And a thought entered into them, as to which of them should be greater.",
  "9:47": "But Jesus, seeing the thoughts of their hearts, took a child and set him beside him,",
  "9:48": "And said to them: Whoever shall receive this child in my name receives me; and whoever shall receive me receives him who sent me. For he who is the least among you all, he is the greatest.",
  "9:49": "And John answered and said: Master, we saw a certain man casting out devils in your name: and we stopped him, because he does not follow with us.",
  "9:50": "And Jesus said to him: Do not stop him: for whoever is not against you is for you.",
  "9:51": "And it happened, when the days of his being taken up were coming to fulfillment, that he steadfastly set his face to go to Jerusalem.",
  "9:52": "And he sent messengers ahead of him: and going, they entered a town of the Samaritans, to prepare for him.",
  "9:53": "And they did not receive him, because his face was set toward Jerusalem.",
  "9:54": "And when his disciples James and John had seen this, they said: Lord, do you want us to command fire to come down from heaven and consume them?",
  "9:55": "And turning, he rebuked them, saying: You do not know of what spirit you are.",
  "9:56": "The Son of man did not come to destroy souls, but to save them. And they went into another town.",
  "9:57": "And it happened, as they walked along the way, that a certain man said to him: I will follow you wherever you go.",
  "9:58": "Jesus said to him: The foxes have holes, and the birds of the air nests: but the Son of man has nowhere to lay his head.",
  "9:59": "But he said to another: Follow me. And he said: Lord, let me first go and bury my father.",
  "9:60": "And Jesus said to him: Let the dead bury their dead: but you go and preach the kingdom of God.",
  "9:61": "And another said: I will follow you, Lord; but let me first say goodbye to those who are at my house.",
  "9:62": "Jesus said to him: No one who puts his hand to the plow and looks back is fit for the kingdom of God.",
  "10:1": "And after these things, the Lord appointed seventy-two others also. And he sent them two by two ahead of him into every city and place where he himself was to come.",
  "10:2": "And he said to them: The harvest indeed is great, but the laborers are few. Pray therefore the Lord of the harvest to send laborers into his harvest.",
  "10:3": "Go: behold, I send you as lambs among wolves.",
  "10:4": "Carry neither purse, nor bag, nor shoes: and greet no one along the way.",
  "10:6": "And if a son of peace is there, your peace shall rest upon him: but if not, it shall return to you.",
  "10:7": "And in the same house remain, eating and drinking what they have: for the laborer is worthy of his wages. Do not move from house to house.",
  "10:8": "And into whatever city you enter, and they receive you, eat what is set before you.",
  "10:9": "And heal the sick who are there and say to them: The kingdom of God has come near to you.",
  "10:10": "But into whatever city you enter, and they do not receive you, go out into its streets and say:",
  "10:11": "Even the very dust of your city that clings to us, we wipe off against you. Yet know this, that the kingdom of God is at hand.",
  "10:12": "I say to you, it shall be more tolerable on that day for Sodom than for that city.",
  "10:13": "Woe to you, Corozain! Woe to you, Bethsaida! For if the mighty works that have been done in you had been done in Tyre and Sidon, they would have done penance long ago, sitting in sackcloth and ashes.",
  "10:15": "And you, Capernaum, who are exalted to heaven, you shall be thrust down to hell.",
  "10:16": "Whoever hears you hears me: and whoever despises you despises me: and whoever despises me despises him who sent me.",
  "10:20": "But do not rejoice in this, that spirits are subject to you: but rejoice in this, that your names are written in heaven.",
  "10:21": "In that same hour, he rejoiced in the Holy Spirit and said: I give praise to you, O Father, Lord of heaven and earth, because you have hidden these things from the wise and prudent and have revealed them to little ones. Yes, Father, for so it has seemed good in your sight.",
  "10:22": "All things have been handed over to me by my Father. And no one knows who the Son is, except the Father: and who the Father is, except the Son and anyone to whom the Son will reveal him.",
  "10:25": "And behold a certain lawyer stood up, testing him and saying: Master, what must I do to possess eternal life?",
  "10:26": "But he said to him: What is written in the law? How do you read it?",
  "10:27": "He answered and said: You shall love the Lord your God with your whole heart and with your whole soul and with all your strength and with all your mind: and your neighbor as yourself.",
  "10:28": "And he said to him: You have answered rightly. Do this: and you shall live.",
  "10:29": "But he, wanting to justify himself, said to Jesus: And who is my neighbor?",
  "10:30": "And Jesus answered and said: A certain man went down from Jerusalem to Jericho and fell among robbers, who stripped him and, having wounded him, went away, leaving him half dead.",
  "10:31": "And it happened that a certain priest was going down the same way: and seeing him, he passed by.",
  "10:32": "In the same way a Levite also, when he was near the place and saw him, passed by.",
  "10:33": "But a certain Samaritan, being on his journey, came near him: and seeing him, he was moved with compassion.",
  "10:34": "And going up to him, he bound up his wounds, pouring in oil and wine: and setting him upon his own animal, he brought him to an inn and took care of him.",
  "10:35": "And the next day he took out two pence and gave them to the innkeeper and said: Take care of him; and whatever more you spend, I will repay you when I return.",
  "10:36": "Which of these three, in your opinion, was a neighbor to him who fell among the robbers?",
  "10:39": "And she had a sister called Mary, who, sitting also at the Lord's feet, listened to his word.",
  "10:40": "But Martha was busy with much serving. And she stood and said: Lord, do you not care that my sister has left me alone to serve? Tell her then to help me.",
  "10:41": "And the Lord answered and said to her: Martha, Martha, you are anxious and troubled about many things:",
  "11:1": "And it happened that as he was praying in a certain place, when he had finished, one of his disciples said to him: Lord, teach us to pray, as John also taught his disciples.",
  "11:5": "And he said to them: Which of you shall have a friend and go to him at midnight and say to him: Friend, lend me three loaves,",
  "11:6": "Because a friend of mine has come to me from his journey and I have nothing to set before him.",
  "11:7": "And he from within should answer and say: Do not bother me; the door is now shut, and my children are with me in bed. I cannot get up and give you anything.",
  "11:8": "Yet if he keeps on knocking, I say to you, although he will not get up and give him anything because he is his friend, yet because of his persistence he will get up and give him as many as he needs.",
  "11:10": "For everyone who asks receives: and whoever seeks finds: and to him who knocks it shall be opened.",
  "11:11": "And which of you, if he asks his father for bread, will give him a stone? Or if he asks for a fish, will give him a serpent instead of a fish?",
  "11:12": "Or if he asks for an egg, will hand him a scorpion?",
  "11:13": "If you then, being evil, know how to give good gifts to your children, how much more will your Father from heaven give the good Spirit to those who ask him?",
  "11:14": "And he was casting out a devil, and it was mute. And when he had cast out the devil, the mute man spoke: and the crowds were amazed at it.",
  "11:16": "And others, testing him, asked him for a sign from heaven.",
  "11:17": "But he, seeing their thoughts, said to them: Every kingdom divided against itself shall be brought to ruin; and house upon house shall fall.",
  "11:18": "And if Satan also is divided against himself, how shall his kingdom stand? For you say that I cast out devils through Beelzebub.",
  "11:20": "But if I cast out devils by the finger of God, surely the kingdom of God has come upon you.",
  "11:21": "When a strong man, armed, guards his courtyard, the things he possesses are in peace.",
  "11:22": "But if one stronger than he comes upon him and overcomes him, he will take away all his armor in which he trusted and will divide up his spoils.",
  "11:23": "Whoever is not with me is against me; and whoever does not gather with me scatters.",
  "11:24": "When the unclean spirit has gone out of a man, he walks through places without water, seeking rest: and not finding any, he says: I will return to my house from where I came out.",
  "11:25": "And when he comes, he finds it swept and put in order.",
  "11:27": "And it happened, as he spoke these things, that a certain woman from the crowd, lifting up her voice, said to him: Blessed is the womb that bore you and the breasts that nursed you.",
  "11:28": "But he said: Yes, rather, blessed are they who hear the word of God and keep it.",
  "11:29": "And as the crowds were gathering, he began to say: This generation is a wicked generation. It asks for a sign: and no sign shall be given it, except the sign of Jonas the prophet.",
  "11:31": "The queen of the south shall rise in the judgment with the men of this generation and shall condemn them: because she came from the ends of the earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon. And behold, something greater than Solomon is here.",
  "11:32": "The men of Ninive shall rise in the judgment with this generation and shall condemn it, because they did penance at the preaching of Jonas. And behold, something greater than Jonas is here.",
  "11:33": "No one lights a candle and puts it in a hidden place, nor under a bushel: but upon a candlestick, so that those who come in may see the light.",
  "11:34": "The light of your body is your eye. If your eye is sound, your whole body will be full of light: but if it is evil, your body also will be full of darkness.",
  "11:35": "Take care, therefore, that the light which is in you is not darkness.",
  "11:36": "If then your whole body is full of light, having no part dark, the whole shall be full of light, as when a bright lamp gives you light.",
  "11:37": "And as he was speaking, a certain Pharisee asked him to dine with him. And he went in and sat down to eat.",
  "11:38": "And the Pharisee began to wonder within himself why he had not washed before dinner.",
  "11:39": "And the Lord said to him: Now you Pharisees make clean the outside of the cup and of the dish: but your inside is full of greed and wickedness.",
  "11:40": "You fools, did not he who made the outside make the inside also?",
  "11:41": "But as for what is within, give alms: and behold, all things are clean to you.",
  "11:42": "But woe to you, Pharisees, because you tithe mint and rue and every herb and pass over judgment and the charity of God. Now these things you ought to have done, and not leave the others undone.",
  "11:43": "Woe to you, Pharisees, because you love the first seats in the synagogues and greetings in the marketplace.",
  "11:44": "Woe to you, because you are like hidden tombs: and men who walk over them are not aware of it.",
  "11:45": "And one of the lawyers answered and said to him: Master, in saying these things, you insult us also.",
  "11:46": "But he said: Woe to you lawyers also, because you load men with burdens which they cannot bear, and you yourselves do not touch the burdens with one of your fingers.",
  "11:47": "Woe to you who build the tombs of the prophets: and your fathers killed them.",
  "11:48": "Truly you bear witness that you approve of the deeds of your fathers. For they indeed killed them: and you build their tombs.",
  "11:49": "For this reason also the wisdom of God said: I will send them prophets and apostles: and some of them they will kill and persecute,",
  "11:51": "From the blood of Abel to the blood of Zacharias, who was slain between the altar and the temple. Yes, I say to you: It shall be required of this generation.",
  "11:52": "Woe to you lawyers, for you have taken away the key of knowledge. You yourselves have not entered in: and those who were entering in, you have hindered.",
  "11:53": "And as he was saying these things to them, the Pharisees and the lawyers began to press him hard and to provoke him to speak about many things,",
  "11:54": "Lying in wait for him and trying to catch something from his mouth, so that they might accuse him.",
  "12:1": "And when great crowds had gathered around him, so that they trod upon one another, he began to say to his disciples: Beware of the leaven of the Pharisees, which is hypocrisy.",
  "12:3": "For whatever you have spoken in darkness shall be made known in the light: and what you have whispered in the ear in inner rooms shall be preached on the housetops.",
  "12:4": "And I say to you, my friends: Do not be afraid of those who kill the body and after that have nothing more that they can do.",
  "12:5": "But I will show you whom you should fear: Fear him who, after he has killed, has power to cast into hell. Yes, I say to you: Fear him.",
  "12:6": "Are not five sparrows sold for two farthings? And not one of them is forgotten before God.",
  "12:7": "Yes, the very hairs of your head are all numbered. Fear not therefore: you are of more value than many sparrows.",
  "12:9": "But whoever shall deny me before men shall be denied before the angels of God.",
  "12:10": "And whoever speaks a word against the Son of man, it shall be forgiven him: but whoever blasphemes against the Holy Spirit, it shall not be forgiven him.",
  "12:11": "And when they bring you into the synagogues and before magistrates and authorities, do not worry about how or what you shall answer, or what you shall say.",
  "12:13": "And one of the crowd said to him: Master, tell my brother to divide the inheritance with me.",
  "12:14": "But he said to him: Man, who has appointed me judge or divider over you?",
  "12:15": "And he said to them: Take care and beware of all greed: for a man's life does not consist in the abundance of things which he possesses.",
  "12:16": "And he told them a parable, saying: The land of a certain rich man brought forth plenty of crops.",
  "12:17": "And he thought within himself, saying: What shall I do, because I have no room in which to store my crops?",
  "12:18": "And he said: This I will do: I will pull down my barns and build bigger ones: and into them I will gather all my crops and my goods.",
  "12:19": "And I will say to my soul: Soul, you have many goods laid up for many years. Take your rest: eat, drink, be merry.",
  "12:20": "But God said to him: You fool, this night your soul is required of you. And whose shall those things be which you have prepared?",
  "12:21": "So is he who lays up treasure for himself and is not rich toward God.",
  "12:22": "And he said to his disciples: Therefore I say to you: Do not worry about your life, what you shall eat, nor about your body, what you shall put on.",
  "12:23": "Life is more than food: and the body is more than clothing.",
  "12:24": "Consider the ravens, for they neither sow nor reap, and they have neither storehouse nor barn, and God feeds them. How much more valuable are you than they?",
  "12:25": "And which of you by worrying can add one cubit to his stature?",
  "12:26": "If then you are not able to do even the least thing, why do you worry about the rest?",
  "12:27": "Consider the lilies, how they grow: they do not labor, nor do they spin. But I say to you, not even Solomon in all his glory was clothed like one of these.",
  "12:28": "Now if God so clothes the grass that is in the field today and tomorrow is cast into the oven, how much more you, O you of little faith?",
  "12:29": "And do not seek what you shall eat or what you shall drink: and do not be lifted up on high.",
  "12:30": "For all these things the nations of the world seek. But your Father knows that you need these things.",
  "12:31": "But seek first the kingdom of God and his justice: and all these things shall be added to you.",
  "12:33": "Sell what you possess and give alms. Make for yourselves purses which do not grow old, a treasure in heaven which does not fail: where no thief comes near, nor moth destroys.",
  "12:35": "Let your loins be girded and lamps burning in your hands.",
  "12:36": "And be like men who wait for their lord, when he shall return from the wedding; so that when he comes and knocks, they may open to him immediately.",
  "12:37": "Blessed are those servants whom the Lord, when he comes, shall find watching. Amen I say to you that he will gird himself and make them sit down at table and will come and serve them.",
  "12:38": "And if he comes in the second watch or comes in the third watch and finds them so, blessed are those servants.",
  "12:39": "But know this: if the master of the house knew at what hour the thief would come, he would surely watch and would not allow his house to be broken into.",
  "12:40": "You also be ready: for the Son of man will come at an hour you do not expect.",
  "12:41": "And Peter said to him: Lord, are you telling this parable to us, or to all?",
  "12:42": "And the Lord said: Who do you think is the faithful and wise steward, whom his lord sets over his household, to give them their measure of wheat at the proper time?",
  "12:43": "Blessed is that servant whom his lord, when he comes, shall find so doing.",
  "12:45": "But if that servant shall say in his heart: My lord is delaying his coming; and shall begin to beat the menservants and maidservants, and to eat and to drink and be drunk:",
  "12:46": "The lord of that servant will come on a day that he does not expect, and at an hour that he does not know: and shall cut him off and shall appoint him his portion with the unbelievers.",
  "12:47": "And that servant who knew the will of his lord and did not prepare himself and did not act according to his will shall be beaten with many stripes.",
  "12:48": "But he who did not know and did things worthy of stripes shall be beaten with few stripes. And to whomever much is given, of him much shall be required: and to whom they have entrusted much, of him they will demand the more.",
  "12:49": "I have come to cast fire on the earth. And what do I desire, but that it be kindled?",
  "12:50": "And I have a baptism with which I am to be baptized. And how distressed I am until it is accomplished!",
  "12:51": "Do you think that I have come to give peace on earth? I tell you, no; but division.",
  "12:52": "For from now on there shall be five in one house divided: three against two, and two against three.",
  "12:54": "And he said also to the crowds: When you see a cloud rising from the west, at once you say: A shower is coming. And so it happens.",
  "12:55": "And when you see the south wind blowing, you say: There will be heat. And it happens.",
  "12:56": "You hypocrites, you know how to read the face of the sky and of the earth: but how is it that you do not read this time?",
  "12:57": "And why do you not judge for yourselves what is just?",
  "12:58": "And when you go with your adversary to the ruler, while you are on the way, try hard to be freed from him: so that he does not drag you to the judge, and the judge hand you over to the officer, and the officer cast you into prison.",
  "12:59": "I say to you, you shall not get out of there until you pay the very last mite.",
  "13:1": "And there were present at that very time some who told him about the Galileans, whose blood Pilate had mixed with their sacrifices.",
  "13:2": "And he answered and said to them: Do you think that these Galileans were worse sinners than all the men of Galilee, because they suffered such things?",
  "13:3": "No, I say to you: but unless you do penance, you shall all likewise perish.",
  "13:4": "Or those eighteen upon whom the tower in Siloe fell and killed them: do you think that they also were debtors above all the men who lived in Jerusalem?",
  "13:5": "No, I say to you: but unless you do penance, you shall all likewise perish.",
  "13:6": "He also told this parable: A certain man had a fig tree planted in his vineyard: and he came looking for fruit on it and found none.",
  "13:7": "And he said to the keeper of the vineyard: Behold, for these three years I have come looking for fruit on this fig tree and I find none. Cut it down therefore. Why should it use up the ground?",
  "13:8": "But he answered and said to him: Lord, leave it alone this year also, until I dig around it and put manure on it.",
  "13:9": "And perhaps it will bear fruit: but if not, then after that you shall cut it down.",
  "13:11": "And behold, there was a woman who had had a spirit of infirmity for eighteen years. And she was bent over and could not look upward at all.",
  "13:12": "When Jesus saw her, he called her to him and said to her: Woman, you are set free from your infirmity.",
  "13:14": "And the ruler of the synagogue, angry that Jesus had healed on the sabbath, said to the crowd: There are six days on which you ought to work. On them therefore come and be healed: and not on the sabbath day.",
  "13:15": "And the Lord answered him and said: You hypocrites, does not each one of you, on the sabbath day, untie his ox or his donkey from the manger and lead them to water?",
  "13:16": "And ought not this daughter of Abraham, whom Satan has bound, behold, these eighteen years, be set free from this bond on the sabbath day?",
  "13:17": "And when he said these things, all his adversaries were put to shame: and all the people rejoiced at all the glorious things that were done by him.",
  "13:18": "He said therefore: What is the kingdom of God like, and to what shall I compare it?",
  "13:19": "It is like a grain of mustard seed, which a man took and cast into his garden: and it grew and became a great tree, and the birds of the air lodged in its branches.",
  "13:20": "And again he said: To what shall I compare the kingdom of God?",
  "13:21": "It is like leaven, which a woman took and hid in three measures of flour, until the whole was leavened.",
  "13:23": "And a certain man said to him: Lord, are only a few saved? But he said to them:",
  "13:25": "But when the master of the house has gone in and shut the door, you shall begin to stand outside and knock at the door, saying: Lord, open to us. And he shall answer and say to you: I do not know where you come from.",
  "13:27": "And he shall say to you: I do not know where you come from. Depart from me, all you workers of iniquity.",
  "13:28": "There shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth, when you see Abraham and Isaac and Jacob and all the prophets in the kingdom of God, and you yourselves thrust out.",
  "13:29": "And they shall come from the east and the west and the north and the south, and shall sit down in the kingdom of God.",
  "13:30": "And behold, there are last who shall be first: and there are first who shall be last.",
  "13:31": "The same day, some of the Pharisees came, saying to him: Depart, and get away from here, for Herod wants to kill you.",
  "13:32": "And he said to them: Go and tell that fox: Behold, I cast out devils and do cures today and tomorrow, and on the third day I am perfected.",
  "13:33": "Nevertheless, I must go on my way today and tomorrow and the day following, because it cannot be that a prophet should perish outside of Jerusalem.",
  "13:34": "Jerusalem, Jerusalem, you who kill the prophets and stone those who are sent to you, how often would I have gathered your children as the bird gathers her brood under her wings, and you would not!",
  "13:35": "Behold, your house shall be left to you desolate. And I say to you that you shall not see me until the time comes when you shall say: Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.",
  "14:1": "And it happened, when Jesus went into the house of one of the Pharisees on the sabbath day, that they were watching him.",
  "14:2": "And behold, there was a certain man before him who had dropsy.",
  "14:3": "And Jesus spoke to the lawyers and Pharisees, saying: Is it lawful to heal on the sabbath day?",
  "14:4": "But they kept silent. And he, taking hold of him, healed him and sent him away.",
  "14:5": "And he answered them and said: Which of you, if his donkey or his ox falls into a pit, will not immediately pull him out on the sabbath day?",
  "14:6": "And they could not answer him about these things.",
  "14:7": "And he also told a parable to those who were invited, noticing how they chose the first seats at the table, saying to them:",
  "14:8": "When you are invited to a wedding, do not sit down in the first place, in case someone more honorable than you has been invited by him,",
  "14:9": "And he who invited you both comes and says to you: Give this man your place. And then you begin with shame to take the lowest place.",
  "14:10": "But when you are invited, go and sit down in the lowest place; so that when he who invited you comes, he may say to you: Friend, go up higher. Then you shall have glory before those who sit at table with you.",
  "14:11": "Because everyone who exalts himself shall be humbled: and whoever humbles himself shall be exalted.",
  "14:12": "And he also said to him who had invited him: When you give a dinner or a supper, do not invite your friends or your brothers or your relatives or your rich neighbors; or else they may invite you in return, and you would be repaid.",
  "14:13": "But when you give a feast, invite the poor, the maimed, the lame and the blind.",
  "14:14": "And you shall be blessed, because they have nothing with which to repay you: for you shall be repaid at the resurrection of the just.",
  "14:15": "When one of those who sat at table with him heard these things, he said to him: Blessed is he who shall eat bread in the kingdom of God.",
  "14:17": "And at the hour of supper he sent his servant to say to those who were invited that they should come: for now all things are ready.",
  "14:18": "And they all began at once to make excuses. The first said to him: I have bought a farm and I must go out and see it. I beg you, hold me excused.",
  "14:19": "And another said: I have bought five yoke of oxen and I am going to try them. I beg you, hold me excused.",
  "14:21": "And the servant returned and told these things to his lord. Then the master of the house, being angry, said to his servant: Go out quickly into the streets and lanes of the city; and bring in here the poor and the feeble and the blind and the lame.",
  "14:22": "And the servant said: Lord, it is done as you have commanded; and still there is room.",
  "14:23": "And the lord said to the servant: Go out into the highways and hedges, and compel them to come in, so that my house may be filled.",
  "14:24": "But I say to you that none of those men who were invited shall taste of my supper.",
  "14:25": "And great crowds went along with him. And turning, he said to them:",
  "14:26": "If anyone comes to me and does not hate his father and mother and wife and children and brothers and sisters, yes, and his own life also, he cannot be my disciple.",
  "14:28": "For which of you, wanting to build a tower, does not first sit down and count the cost, whether he has enough to finish it,",
  "14:29": "So that, after he has laid the foundation and is not able to finish it, all who see it do not begin to mock him,",
  "14:31": "Or what king, about to go to make war against another king, does not first sit down and consider whether he is able, with ten thousand, to meet him who comes against him with twenty thousand?",
  "14:32": "Or else, while the other is still far away, he sends messengers and asks for terms of peace.",
  "14:33": "So likewise, every one of you who does not renounce all that he possesses cannot be my disciple.",
  "14:34": "Salt is good. But if the salt loses its taste, with what shall it be seasoned?",
  "14:35": "It is fit neither for the land nor for the dunghill: but it shall be thrown out. Whoever has ears to hear, let him hear.",
  "15:1": "Now the tax collectors and sinners were coming near to him to hear him.",
  "15:3": "And he told them this parable, saying:",
  "15:4": "What man of you who has a hundred sheep, if he loses one of them, does not leave the ninety-nine in the desert and go after the one which was lost, until he finds it?",
  "15:5": "And when he has found it, does he not lay it upon his shoulders, rejoicing?",
  "15:6": "And coming home, does he not call together his friends and neighbors, saying to them: Rejoice with me, because I have found my sheep that was lost?",
  "15:7": "I say to you that even so there shall be joy in heaven upon one sinner who does penance, more than upon ninety-nine just who need not penance.",
  "15:8": "Or what woman having ten coins, if she loses one coin, does not light a candle and sweep the house and search carefully until she finds it?",
  "15:9": "And when she has found it, does she not call together her friends and neighbors, saying: Rejoice with me, because I have found the coin which I had lost?",
  "15:10": "So I say to you, there shall be joy before the angels of God upon one sinner doing penance.",
  "15:12": "And the younger of them said to his father: Father, give me the share of the property that falls to me. And he divided his property between them.",
  "15:13": "And not many days after, the younger son, gathering everything together, went abroad into a far country: and there he wasted his property, living recklessly.",
  "15:14": "And after he had spent everything, a great famine came in that country: and he began to be in need.",
  "15:15": "And he went and attached himself to one of the citizens of that country. And he sent him into his farm to feed swine.",
  "15:16": "And he would gladly have filled his belly with the husks the swine ate: and no one gave him anything.",
  "15:17": "And coming to himself, he said: How many hired servants in my father's house have plenty of bread, and here I am perishing with hunger!",
  "15:20": "And rising up, he came to his father. And when he was still a great way off, his father saw him and was moved with compassion and, running to him, fell upon his neck and kissed him.",
  "15:21": "And the son said to him: Father, I have sinned against heaven and before you. I am no longer worthy to be called your son.",
  "15:22": "And the father said to his servants: Quickly bring out the best robe and put it on him: and put a ring on his hand and shoes on his feet.",
  "15:23": "And bring the fatted calf here, and kill it: and let us eat and make merry:",
  "15:24": "Because this my son was dead and has come to life again, was lost and is found. And they began to make merry.",
  "15:25": "Now his elder son was in the field, and when he came and drew near to the house, he heard music and dancing.",
  "15:26": "And he called one of the servants and asked what these things meant.",
  "15:27": "And he said to him: Your brother has come and your father has killed the fatted calf, because he has received him safe.",
  "15:28": "And he was angry and would not go in. His father therefore came out and began to plead with him.",
  "15:29": "And he answered and said to his father: Behold, for so many years I have served you and I have never disobeyed your commandment: and yet you have never given me a young goat to make merry with my friends.",
  "15:30": "But as soon as this son of yours has come, who has devoured his property with harlots, you have killed the fatted calf for him.",
  "15:32": "But it was right that we should make merry and be glad: for this your brother was dead and has come to life again; he was lost, and is found.",
  "16:1": "And he also said to his disciples: There was a certain rich man who had a steward: and the steward was accused to him of wasting his goods.",
  "16:2": "And he called him and said to him: What is this I hear about you? Give an account of your stewardship: for you can be steward no longer.",
  "16:3": "And the steward said within himself: What shall I do, because my lord is taking the stewardship away from me? I am not strong enough to dig; I am ashamed to beg.",
  "16:4": "I know what I will do, so that when I am removed from the stewardship, they may receive me into their houses.",
  "16:5": "Therefore, calling together each one of his lord's debtors, he said to the first: How much do you owe my lord?",
  "16:6": "And he said: A hundred barrels of oil. And he said to him: Take your bill and sit down quickly and write fifty.",
  "16:7": "Then he said to another: And how much do you owe? And he said: A hundred measures of wheat. He said to him: Take your bill and write eighty.",
  "16:8": "And the lord praised the unjust steward because he had acted shrewdly: for the children of this world are shrewder in their generation than the children of light.",
  "16:9": "And I say to you: Make friends for yourselves with the mammon of iniquity: so that when you fail, they may receive you into everlasting dwellings.",
  "16:10": "Whoever is faithful in what is least is faithful also in what is greater: and whoever is unjust in what is little is unjust also in what is greater.",
  "16:11": "If then you have not been faithful in the unjust mammon, who will trust you with what is true?",
  "16:12": "And if you have not been faithful in what belongs to another, who will give you what is your own?",
  "16:14": "Now the Pharisees, who were greedy, heard all these things: and they mocked him.",
  "16:15": "And he said to them: You are the ones who justify yourselves before men, but God knows your hearts. For what is highly esteemed among men is an abomination before God.",
  "16:16": "The law and the prophets were until John. From that time the kingdom of God is preached: and everyone uses force to enter it.",
  "16:17": "And it is easier for heaven and earth to pass away than for one tittle of the law to fail.",
  "16:18": "Everyone who puts away his wife and marries another commits adultery: and whoever marries her who is put away from her husband commits adultery.",
  "16:19": "There was a certain rich man who was clothed in purple and fine linen and feasted splendidly every day.",
  "16:21": "Longing to be filled with the crumbs that fell from the rich man's table. And no one gave him any: moreover, the dogs came and licked his sores.",
  "16:23": "And lifting up his eyes when he was in torments, he saw Abraham far off and Lazarus in his bosom:",
  "16:25": "And Abraham said to him: Son, remember that you received good things in your lifetime, and likewise Lazarus evil things: but now he is comforted and you are tormented.",
  "16:26": "And besides all this, between us and you there is fixed a great chasm: so that those who would pass from here to you cannot, nor can anyone cross from there to us.",
  "16:27": "And he said: Then, father, I beg you to send him to my father's house,",
  "16:28": "For I have five brothers, so that he may warn them, and they also may not come into this place of torments.",
  "16:30": "But he said: No, father Abraham: but if one went to them from the dead, they will do penance.",
  "16:31": "And he said to him: If they do not hear Moses and the prophets, neither will they believe if one rises again from the dead.",
  "17:2": "It would be better for him if a millstone were hung around his neck and he were thrown into the sea, than that he should scandalize one of these little ones.",
  "17:3": "Take care of yourselves. If your brother sins against you, rebuke him: and if he does penance, forgive him.",
  "17:4": "And if he sins against you seven times in a day, and seven times in a day turns back to you, saying: I repent: forgive him.",
  "17:6": "And the Lord said: If you had faith like a grain of mustard seed, you might say to this mulberry tree: Be uprooted and be planted in the sea. And it would obey you.",
  "17:7": "But which of you, having a servant plowing or tending cattle, will say to him when he has come in from the field: Come at once and sit down at table?",
  "17:8": "And will he not rather say to him: Prepare my supper and gird yourself and serve me while I eat and drink; and afterwards you shall eat and drink?",
  "17:10": "I think not. So you also, when you have done all the things that are commanded you, say: We are unprofitable servants; we have done what we ought to do.",
  "17:11": "And it happened, as he was going to Jerusalem, that he passed through the midst of Samaria and Galilee.",
  "17:12": "And as he entered a certain town, ten men who were lepers met him, who stood far off.",
  "17:13": "And they lifted up their voice, saying: Jesus, Master, have mercy on us.",
  "17:14": "When he saw them, he said: Go, show yourselves to the priests. And it happened, as they went, that they were made clean.",
  "17:15": "And one of them, when he saw that he was made clean, went back, glorifying God with a loud voice.",
  "17:16": "And he fell on his face at his feet, giving thanks. And this man was a Samaritan.",
  "17:17": "And Jesus answered and said: Were not ten made clean? And where are the nine?",
  "17:18": "Was no one found to return and give glory to God, except this foreigner?",
  "17:20": "And being asked by the Pharisees when the kingdom of God would come, he answered them and said: The kingdom of God does not come with observation.",
  "17:21": "Nor shall they say: Behold here, or behold there. For behold, the kingdom of God is within you.",
  "17:23": "And they will say to you: See here, and see there. Do not go after them, nor follow them.",
  "17:24": "For as the lightning that flashes from under heaven shines to the parts that are under heaven, so shall the Son of man be in his day.",
  "17:27": "They ate and drank, they married wives and were given in marriage, until the day that Noe entered the ark and the flood came and destroyed them all.",
  "17:28": "Likewise as it happened in the days of Lot: they ate and drank, they bought and sold, they planted and built.",
  "17:29": "And on the day that Lot went out of Sodom, it rained fire and brimstone from heaven and destroyed them all.",
  "17:30": "In the same way it shall be on the day when the Son of man shall be revealed.",
  "17:31": "In that hour, whoever is on the housetop, with his goods in the house, let him not go down to take them away: and whoever is in the field, likewise, let him not turn back.",
  "17:33": "Whoever shall seek to save his life shall lose it: and whoever shall lose it shall preserve it.",
  "17:36": "They answered and said to him: Where, Lord?",
  "17:37": "And he said to them: Wherever the body is, there the eagles also will be gathered together.",
  "18:1": "And he also told them a parable, that they ought always to pray and not lose heart,",
  "18:2": "Saying: There was a judge in a certain city, who did not fear God nor respect man.",
  "18:3": "And there was a certain widow in that city; and she kept coming to him, saying: Give me justice against my adversary.",
  "18:4": "And for a long time he would not. But afterwards he said within himself: Although I do not fear God nor respect man,",
  "18:5": "Yet because this widow troubles me, I will give her justice, so that she does not wear me out by her continual coming.",
  "18:7": "And will not God give justice to his elect who cry to him day and night? And will he be slow to help them?",
  "18:8": "I say to you that he will quickly give them justice. But yet, when the Son of man comes, do you think he shall find faith on earth?",
  "18:9": "And to some who trusted in themselves as just and despised others, he also told this parable:",
  "18:10": "Two men went up into the temple to pray: the one a Pharisee and the other a tax collector.",
  "18:11": "The Pharisee, standing, prayed thus with himself: O God, I give you thanks that I am not like the rest of men, robbers, unjust, adulterers, or even like this tax collector.",
  "18:13": "And the tax collector, standing far off, would not even lift up his eyes toward heaven; but struck his breast, saying: O God, be merciful to me, a sinner.",
  "18:14": "I say to you, this man went down to his house justified rather than the other: because everyone who exalts himself shall be humbled: and whoever humbles himself shall be exalted.",
  "18:15": "And they also brought infants to him, so that he might touch them. When the disciples saw it, they rebuked them.",
  "18:16": "But Jesus, calling them together, said: Let the children come to me and do not forbid them: for of such is the kingdom of God.",
  "18:18": "And a certain ruler asked him, saying: Good master, what shall I do to possess everlasting life?",
  "18:19": "And Jesus said to him: Why do you call me good? No one is good but God alone.",
  "18:21": "And he said: All these things I have kept from my youth.",
  "18:22": "When Jesus heard this, he said to him: One thing is still lacking to you. Sell everything you have and give to the poor: and you shall have treasure in heaven. And come, follow me.",
  "18:23": "When he heard these things, he became sorrowful: for he was very rich.",
  "18:24": "And Jesus, seeing him become sorrowful, said: How hard it is for those who have riches to enter into the kingdom of God!",
  "18:26": "And those who heard it said: Who then can be saved?",
  "18:29": "And he said to them: Amen, I say to you, there is no one who has left home or parents or brothers or wife or children for the sake of the kingdom of God,",
  "18:31": "Then Jesus took the twelve aside and said to them: Behold, we are going up to Jerusalem; and all things shall be accomplished which were written by the prophets about the Son of man.",
  "18:32": "For he shall be handed over to the Gentiles and shall be mocked and scourged and spit upon.",
  "18:33": "And after they have scourged him, they will put him to death. And on the third day he shall rise again.",
  "18:34": "And they understood none of these things, and this word was hidden from them: and they did not understand the things that were said.",
  "18:35": "Now it happened, as he drew near to Jericho, that a certain blind man was sitting by the wayside, begging.",
  "18:36": "And when he heard the crowd passing by, he asked what this meant.",
  "18:39": "And those who went ahead rebuked him, telling him to be quiet: but he cried out much more: Son of David, have mercy on me.",
  "18:40": "And Jesus, standing still, commanded him to be brought to him. And when he had come near, he asked him,",
  "18:41": "Saying: What do you want me to do for you? And he said: Lord, that I may see.",
  "18:42": "And Jesus said to him: Receive your sight: your faith has made you whole.",
  "19:1": "And entering, he walked through Jericho.",
  "19:3": "And he tried to see who Jesus was: and he could not because of the crowd, because he was short.",
  "19:4": "And running ahead, he climbed up into a sycamore tree, so that he might see him: for he was about to pass that way.",
  "19:5": "And when Jesus came to the place, looking up, he saw him and said to him: Zacheus, hurry and come down: for today I must stay in your house.",
  "19:6": "And he hurried and came down and received him with joy.",
  "19:7": "And when all saw it, they murmured, saying that he had gone to be the guest of a man who was a sinner.",
  "19:8": "But Zacheus, standing, said to the Lord: Behold, Lord, half of my goods I give to the poor; and if I have cheated anyone of anything, I repay him fourfold.",
  "19:9": "Jesus said to him: Today salvation has come to this house, because he also is a son of Abraham.",
  "19:10": "For the Son of man has come to seek and to save what was lost.",
  "19:11": "As they were hearing these things, he went on to tell a parable, because he was near Jerusalem and because they thought that the kingdom of God would appear immediately.",
  "19:12": "He said therefore: A certain nobleman went into a far country to receive for himself a kingdom and to return.",
  "19:13": "And calling his ten servants, he gave them ten pounds and said to them: Trade until I come.",
  "19:14": "But his citizens hated him, and they sent messengers after him, saying: We will not have this man to reign over us.",
  "19:15": "And it happened that he returned, having received the kingdom: and he ordered the servants to whom he had given the money to be called, so that he might know how much each one had gained by trading.",
  "19:16": "And the first came, saying: Lord, your pound has gained ten pounds.",
  "19:17": "And he said to him: Well done, good servant; because you have been faithful in a little, you shall have authority over ten cities.",
  "19:20": "And another came, saying: Lord, behold, here is your pound, which I have kept laid away in a cloth.",
  "19:21": "For I feared you, because you are a severe man: you take up what you did not lay down: and you reap what you did not sow.",
  "19:22": "He said to him: Out of your own mouth I judge you, you wicked servant. You knew that I was a severe man, taking up what I did not lay down and reaping what I did not sow.",
  "19:23": "Why then did you not put my money in the bank, so that at my coming I might have collected it with interest?",
  "19:24": "And he said to those who stood by: Take the pound away from him and give it to him who has ten pounds.",
  "19:26": "But I say to you that to everyone who has shall be given, and he shall have abundance: and from him who has not, even what he has shall be taken from him.",
  "19:28": "And having said these things, he went on ahead, going up to Jerusalem.",
  "19:29": "And it happened, when he had come near to Bethphage and Bethania, to the mount called Olivet, that he sent two of his disciples,",
  "19:30": "Saying: Go into the town which is opposite you, and as you enter it you shall find a colt tied, on which no one has ever sat: untie him and bring him here.",
  "19:31": "And if anyone asks you: Why are you untying him? You shall say this to him: Because the Lord has need of him.",
  "19:32": "And those who were sent went their way and found the colt standing, just as he had told them.",
  "19:33": "And as they were untying the colt, its owners said to them: Why are you untying the colt?",
  "19:35": "And they brought him to Jesus. And throwing their garments on the colt, they set Jesus on it.",
  "19:36": "And as he went, they spread their clothes underneath him on the road.",
  "19:37": "And when he was now coming near the descent of Mount Olivet, the whole crowd of his disciples began with joy to praise God with a loud voice for all the mighty works they had seen,",
  "19:39": "And some of the Pharisees from among the crowd said to him: Master, rebuke your disciples.",
  "19:40": "And he said to them: I say to you that if these keep silent, the stones will cry out.",
  "19:42": "If you also had known, even in this your day, the things that are for your peace! But now they are hidden from your eyes.",
  "19:43": "For the days shall come upon you when your enemies shall cast up a trench around you and surround you and close you in on every side,",
  "19:44": "And beat you flat to the ground, and your children who are in you. And they shall not leave in you a stone upon a stone: because you have not known the time of your visitation.",
  "19:45": "And entering into the temple, he began to drive out those who sold in it and those who bought,",
  "19:47": "And he was teaching daily in the temple. And the chief priests and the scribes and the leaders of the people were seeking to destroy him.",
  "19:48": "And they could not find what to do to him: for all the people were hanging on his words.",
  "20:1": "And it happened on one of the days, as he was teaching the people in the temple and preaching the gospel, that the chief priests and the scribes, with the ancients, came together",
  "20:2": "And spoke to him, saying: Tell us, by what authority are you doing these things? Or, who is it that has given you this authority?",
  "20:3": "And Jesus answered and said to them: I will also ask you one thing. Answer me:",
  "20:4": "The baptism of John, was it from heaven, or from men?",
  "20:5": "But they reasoned among themselves, saying: If we say, From heaven, he will say: Why then did you not believe him?",
  "20:6": "But if we say, From men, the whole people will stone us. For they are convinced that John was a prophet.",
  "20:7": "And they answered that they did not know where it was from.",
  "20:9": "And he began to tell the people this parable: A certain man planted a vineyard and leased it to tenants: and he was away for a long time.",
  "20:10": "And at the right season he sent a servant to the tenants, so that they would give him some of the fruit of the vineyard. But they beat him and sent him away empty-handed.",
  "20:11": "And again he sent another servant. But they beat him also and, treating him shamefully, sent him away empty-handed.",
  "20:12": "And again he sent a third: and they wounded him also and threw him out.",
  "20:13": "Then the lord of the vineyard said: What shall I do? I will send my beloved son. Perhaps, when they see him, they will respect him.",
  "20:14": "But when the tenants saw him, they reasoned among themselves, saying: This is the heir. Let us kill him, so that the inheritance may be ours.",
  "20:15": "So throwing him out of the vineyard, they killed him. What therefore will the lord of the vineyard do to them?",
  "20:16": "He will come and will destroy these tenants and will give the vineyard to others. When they heard this, they said to him: God forbid.",
  "20:17": "But he, looking at them, said: What then is this that is written: The stone which the builders rejected has become the head of the corner?",
  "20:18": "Whoever falls upon that stone shall be broken: and upon whomever it falls, it will grind him to powder.",
  "20:19": "And the chief priests and the scribes tried to lay hands on him that same hour: but they feared the people, for they knew that he had spoken this parable against them.",
  "20:20": "And watching him closely, they sent spies who pretended to be just, so that they might catch him in his words and hand him over to the authority and power of the governor.",
  "20:21": "And they asked him, saying: Master, we know that you speak and teach rightly: and you do not show favor to anyone, but teach the way of God in truth.",
  "20:22": "Is it lawful for us to give tribute to Caesar, or not?",
  "20:23": "But he, seeing their cunning, said to them: Why do you test me?",
  "20:24": "Show me a penny. Whose image and inscription does it have? They answered and said to him: Caesar's.",
  "20:25": "And he said to them: Render therefore to Caesar the things that are Caesar's: and to God the things that are God's.",
  "20:26": "And they could not find fault with his word before the people: and wondering at his answer, they kept silent.",
  "20:27": "And some of the Sadducees, who deny that there is any resurrection, came to him: and they asked him,",
  "20:28": "Saying: Master, Moses wrote for us: If any man's brother dies, having a wife, and he leaves no children, his brother should take her as his wife and raise up offspring for his brother.",
  "20:29": "There were therefore seven brothers: and the first took a wife and died without children.",
  "20:30": "And the next took her as his wife: and he also died childless.",
  "20:31": "And the third took her. And in the same way all the seven: and they left no children and died.",
  "20:33": "In the resurrection therefore, whose wife of them shall she be? For all seven had her as wife.",
  "20:35": "But those who shall be counted worthy of that world and of the resurrection from the dead shall neither marry nor be given in marriage.",
  "20:36": "Nor can they die any more, for they are equal to the angels and are the children of God, being the children of the resurrection.",
  "20:37": "Now that the dead rise again, Moses also showed at the bush, when he called the Lord the God of Abraham and the God of Isaac and the God of Jacob.",
  "20:39": "And some of the scribes answered and said to him: Master, you have spoken well.",
  "20:40": "And after that they did not dare to ask him any more questions.",
  "20:41": "But he said to them: How do they say that the Christ is the son of David?",
  "20:42": "And David himself says in the book of Psalms: The Lord said to my Lord, sit at my right hand,",
  "20:43": "Until I make your enemies your footstool.",
  "20:46": "Beware of the scribes, who like to walk in long robes and love greetings in the marketplace and the first chairs in the synagogues and the places of honor at feasts:",
  "20:47": "Who devour the houses of widows, making long prayers for show. These shall receive greater damnation.",
  "21:1": "And looking up, he saw the rich men putting their gifts into the treasury.",
  "21:2": "And he also saw a certain poor widow putting in two small copper coins.",
  "21:3": "And he said: Truly I say to you that this poor widow has put in more than all of them.",
  "21:4": "For all these have put into the offerings of God out of their abundance: but she out of her poverty has put in all the living that she had.",
  "21:5": "And when some were saying of the temple that it was adorned with fine stones and gifts, he said:",
  "21:6": "As for these things which you see, the days will come in which there shall not be left a stone upon a stone that shall not be thrown down.",
  "21:7": "And they asked him, saying: Master, when shall these things be? And what shall be the sign when they begin to happen?",
  "21:8": "And he said: Take care that you are not led astray: for many will come in my name, saying: I am he, and the time is at hand. Do not go after them, therefore.",
  "21:9": "And when you hear of wars and uprisings, do not be terrified. These things must first happen: but the end is not yet.",
  "21:11": "And there shall be great earthquakes in various places and plagues and famines and terrors from heaven: and there shall be great signs.",
  "21:12": "But before all these things, they will lay their hands on you and persecute you, handing you over to the synagogues and into prisons, dragging you before kings and governors for my name's sake.",
  "21:13": "And it shall turn out for you as a testimony.",
  "21:14": "Settle it therefore in your hearts not to think beforehand how you shall answer:",
  "21:15": "For I will give you a mouth and wisdom which all your adversaries shall not be able to resist or contradict.",
  "21:16": "And you shall be betrayed by your parents and brothers and relatives and friends: and some of you they will put to death.",
  "21:20": "And when you see Jerusalem surrounded by an army, then know that its desolation is at hand.",
  "21:21": "Then let those who are in Judea flee to the mountains: and let those who are in the midst of it depart: and let those who are in the countryside not enter into it.",
  "21:22": "For these are the days of vengeance, so that all things that are written may be fulfilled.",
  "21:23": "But woe to those who are with child and those who are nursing in those days: for there shall be great distress in the land and wrath upon this people.",
  "21:24": "And they shall fall by the edge of the sword and shall be led away captive into all nations: and Jerusalem shall be trodden down by the Gentiles until the times of the nations are fulfilled.",
  "21:25": "And there shall be signs in the sun and in the moon and in the stars; and upon the earth distress of nations, because of the confusion of the roaring of the sea and of the waves:",
  "21:26": "Men fainting for fear and expectation of what shall come upon the whole world. For the powers of heaven shall be shaken.",
  "21:28": "But when these things begin to happen, look up and lift up your heads, because your redemption is at hand.",
  "21:29": "And he told them a parable: See the fig tree and all the trees:",
  "21:30": "When they now put forth their fruit, you know that summer is near;",
  "21:31": "So you also, when you see these things happen, know that the kingdom of God is at hand.",
  "21:32": "Amen, I say to you, this generation shall not pass away until all things are fulfilled.",
  "21:34": "And take care of yourselves, so that your hearts are not weighed down with overindulgence and drunkenness and the cares of this life, and that day come upon you suddenly.",
  "21:35": "For like a snare it shall come upon all who dwell upon the face of the whole earth.",
  "21:36": "Watch, therefore, praying at all times, so that you may be counted worthy to escape all these things that are to come and to stand before the Son of man.",
  "21:37": "And in the daytime he was teaching in the temple: but at night he went out and stayed on the mount that is called Olivet.",
  "22:2": "And the chief priests and the scribes were seeking how they might put Jesus to death: but they feared the people.",
  "22:3": "And Satan entered into Judas, who was called Iscariot, one of the twelve.",
  "22:4": "And he went and talked with the chief priests and the officers about how he might betray him to them.",
  "22:5": "And they were glad and agreed to give him money.",
  "22:6": "And he promised. And he looked for an opportunity to betray him in the absence of the crowd.",
  "22:7": "And the day of the unleavened bread came, on which the pasch had to be killed.",
  "22:8": "And he sent Peter and John, saying: Go and prepare the pasch for us, so that we may eat.",
  "22:9": "But they said: Where do you want us to prepare it?",
  "22:10": "And he said to them: Behold, as you go into the city, a man carrying a pitcher of water shall meet you: follow him into the house which he enters.",
  "22:11": "And you shall say to the master of the house: The master says to you: Where is the guest room, where I may eat the pasch with my disciples?",
  "22:12": "And he will show you a large dining room, furnished. Prepare it there.",
  "22:13": "And they went and found it as he had said to them and made ready the pasch.",
  "22:14": "And when the hour had come, he sat down at table, and the twelve apostles with him.",
  "22:16": "For I say to you that from this time I will not eat it until it is fulfilled in the kingdom of God.",
  "22:18": "For I say to you that I will not drink of the fruit of the vine until the kingdom of God comes.",
  "22:19": "And taking bread, he gave thanks and broke it and gave it to them, saying: This is my body, which is given for you. Do this for a commemoration of me.",
  "22:20": "In the same way the chalice also, after he had eaten supper, saying: This is the chalice, the new testament in my blood, which shall be shed for you.",
  "22:21": "But yet behold, the hand of him who betrays me is with me on the table.",
  "22:22": "And the Son of man indeed goes, according to what has been determined: but yet, woe to that man by whom he shall be betrayed.",
  "22:23": "And they began to ask among themselves which of them it was who would do this thing.",
  "22:24": "And there was also a dispute among them as to which of them should be thought the greatest.",
  "22:25": "And he said to them: The kings of the Gentiles lord it over them; and those who have power over them are called benefactors.",
  "22:26": "But you, not so: but let him who is the greatest among you become as the youngest: and him who is the leader, as one who serves.",
  "22:27": "For which is greater, he who sits at table or he who serves? Is it not he who sits at table? But I am in your midst as one who serves.",
  "22:28": "And you are the ones who have stayed with me in my trials:",
  "22:29": "And I appoint to you, as my Father has appointed to me, a kingdom;",
  "22:30": "So that you may eat and drink at my table in my kingdom: and may sit upon thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel.",
  "22:31": "And the Lord said: Simon, Simon, behold, Satan has desired to have you, so that he may sift you as wheat.",
  "22:32": "But I have prayed for you, that your faith may not fail: and you, once you have turned back, strengthen your brothers.",
  "22:33": "And he said to him: Lord, I am ready to go with you both to prison and to death.",
  "22:34": "And he said: I say to you, Peter, the cock shall not crow this day until you deny three times that you know me. And he said to them:",
  "22:35": "When I sent you without purse and bag and shoes, did you lack anything?",
  "22:36": "But they said: Nothing. Then he said to them: But now whoever has a purse, let him take it, and likewise a bag: and whoever has none, let him sell his coat and buy a sword.",
  "22:37": "For I say to you that what is written must yet be fulfilled in me: And he was counted among the wicked. For the things concerning me are coming to an end.",
  "22:39": "And going out, he went, as was his custom, to the Mount of Olives. And his disciples also followed him.",
  "22:40": "And when he had come to the place, he said to them: Pray, so that you do not enter into temptation.",
  "22:41": "And he withdrew from them about a stone's throw. And kneeling down, he prayed,",
  "22:43": "And an angel from heaven appeared to him, strengthening him. And being in agony, he prayed more earnestly.",
  "22:44": "And his sweat became like drops of blood, trickling down upon the ground.",
  "22:45": "And when he rose up from prayer and had come to the disciples, he found them sleeping for sorrow.",
  "22:46": "And he said to them: Why are you sleeping? Arise: pray, so that you do not enter into temptation.",
  "22:47": "While he was still speaking, behold a crowd; and he who was called Judas, one of the twelve, went ahead of them and came near to Jesus to kiss him.",
  "22:49": "And those who were around him, seeing what was about to happen, said to him: Lord, shall we strike with the sword?",
  "22:51": "But Jesus answered and said: Let them go this far. And when he had touched his ear, he healed him.",
  "22:52": "And Jesus said to the chief priests and officers of the temple and the ancients, who had come to him: Have you come out, as against a thief, with swords and clubs?",
  "22:53": "When I was daily with you in the temple, you did not stretch out your hands against me: but this is your hour and the power of darkness.",
  "22:54": "And seizing him, they led him to the high priest's house. But Peter followed at a distance.",
  "22:55": "And when they had kindled a fire in the middle of the courtyard and were sitting around it, Peter was in the midst of them.",
  "22:56": "When a certain servant girl saw him sitting by the light and had looked at him closely, she said: This man also was with him.",
  "22:58": "And after a little while, another, seeing him, said: You also are one of them. But Peter said: Man, I am not.",
  "22:59": "And after about the space of one hour, another man insisted, saying: Truly this man also was with him: for he is also a Galilean.",
  "22:60": "And Peter said: Man, I do not know what you are saying. And immediately, while he was still speaking, the cock crowed.",
  "22:61": "And the Lord turned and looked at Peter. And Peter remembered the word of the Lord, how he had said: Before the cock crows, you shall deny me three times.",
  "22:62": "And Peter went out and wept bitterly.",
  "22:63": "And the men who held him mocked him and beat him.",
  "22:64": "And they blindfolded him and struck his face. And they asked him, saying: Prophesy: Who is it that struck you?",
  "22:65": "And blaspheming, they said many other things against him.",
  "22:66": "And as soon as it was day, the ancients of the people and the chief priests and scribes came together. And they brought him into their council, saying: If you are the Christ, tell us.",
  "22:67": "And he said to them: If I tell you, you will not believe me.",
  "22:68": "And if I also ask you, you will not answer me, nor let me go.",
  "22:69": "But from now on the Son of man shall be seated at the right hand of the power of God.",
  "22:70": "Then they all said: Are you then the Son of God? And he said: You say that I am.",
  "22:71": "And they said: What further testimony do we need? For we ourselves have heard it from his own mouth.",
  "23:1": "And the whole crowd of them rose up and led him to Pilate.",
  "23:2": "And they began to accuse him, saying: We have found this man misleading our nation and forbidding tribute to be given to Caesar and saying that he is Christ the king.",
  "23:3": "And Pilate asked him, saying: Are you the king of the Jews? And he answered and said: You say it.",
  "23:4": "And Pilate said to the chief priests and to the crowds: I find no cause in this man.",
  "23:5": "But they insisted all the more, saying: He stirs up the people, teaching throughout all Judea, beginning from Galilee to this place.",
  "23:6": "But when Pilate heard Galilee, he asked whether the man was a Galilean.",
  "23:7": "And when he learned that he belonged to Herod's jurisdiction, he sent him to Herod, who was himself also in Jerusalem in those days.",
  "23:8": "And Herod, seeing Jesus, was very glad: for he had wanted to see him for a long time, because he had heard many things about him; and he hoped to see some sign done by him.",
  "23:9": "And he questioned him with many words. But he answered him nothing.",
  "23:11": "And Herod with his soldiers treated him with contempt and mocked him, putting a white garment on him: and sent him back to Pilate.",
  "23:12": "And Herod and Pilate became friends that same day: for before they had been enemies to one another.",
  "23:13": "And Pilate, calling together the chief priests and the rulers and the people,",
  "23:14": "Said to them: You have brought this man to me as one who misleads the people. And behold, I, having examined him before you, find no cause in this man in the things of which you accuse him.",
  "23:15": "No, nor did Herod either. For I sent you to him: and behold, nothing worthy of death has been done by him.",
  "23:16": "I will punish him therefore and release him.",
  "23:17": "Now he was obliged to release one to them at the feast day.",
  "23:18": "But the whole crowd cried out together, saying: Away with this man, and release to us Barabbas:",
  "23:19": "Who had been thrown into prison for a certain uprising made in the city and for a murder.",
  "23:20": "And Pilate spoke to them again, wanting to release Jesus.",
  "23:22": "And he said to them the third time: Why, what evil has this man done? I find no cause of death in him. I will punish him therefore and let him go.",
  "23:23": "But they kept insisting with loud voices, demanding that he be crucified. And their voices prevailed.",
  "23:24": "And Pilate gave sentence that what they demanded should be done.",
  "23:25": "And he released to them the one who had been thrown into prison for murder and uprising, whom they had asked for. But Jesus he handed over to their will.",
  "23:26": "And as they led him away, they seized a certain Simon of Cyrene, coming from the country; and they laid the cross on him to carry behind Jesus.",
  "23:27": "And a great crowd of people followed him, and of women, who were mourning and lamenting him.",
  "23:28": "But Jesus, turning to them, said: Daughters of Jerusalem, do not weep over me; but weep for yourselves and for your children.",
  "23:29": "For behold, the days shall come in which they will say: Blessed are the barren and the wombs that have not borne and the breasts that have not nursed.",
  "23:30": "Then they shall begin to say to the mountains: Fall upon us. And to the hills: Cover us.",
  "23:32": "And two others, who were criminals, were also led with him to be put to death.",
  "23:33": "And when they had come to the place which is called Calvary, they crucified him there: and the robbers, one on the right hand and the other on the left.",
  "23:35": "And the people stood watching. And the rulers with them mocked him, saying: He saved others: let him save himself, if he is the Christ, the chosen of God.",
  "23:38": "And there was also an inscription written over him in letters of Greek and Latin and Hebrew: THIS IS THE KING OF THE JEWS.",
  "23:39": "And one of those robbers who were hanged blasphemed him, saying: If you are the Christ, save yourself and us.",
  "23:40": "But the other answered and rebuked him, saying: Do you not even fear God, seeing you are under the same condemnation?",
  "23:41": "And we indeed justly: for we are receiving the due reward of our deeds. But this man has done no evil.",
  "23:42": "And he said to Jesus: Lord, remember me when you come into your kingdom.",
  "23:45": "And the sun was darkened, and the veil of the temple was torn in the middle.",
  "23:46": "And Jesus, crying out with a loud voice, said: Father, into your hands I commend my spirit. And saying this, he gave up the ghost.",
  "23:47": "Now the centurion, seeing what had happened, glorified God, saying: Indeed this was a just man.",
  "23:48": "And all the crowd of those who had come together to that sight and saw the things that were done returned, striking their breasts.",
  "23:49": "And all who knew him, and the women who had followed him from Galilee, stood far off, watching these things.",
  "23:50": "And behold, there was a man named Joseph, who was a member of the council, a good and just man,",
  "23:51": "(He had not consented to their plan and their deeds) of Arimathea, a city of Judea: who himself was also waiting for the kingdom of God.",
  "23:52": "This man went to Pilate and asked for the body of Jesus.",
  "23:53": "And taking him down, he wrapped him in fine linen and laid him in a tomb that was cut in stone, in which no one had ever yet been laid.",
  "23:54": "And it was the day of the Parasceve: and the sabbath was drawing near.",
  "23:55": "And the women who had come with him from Galilee followed after and saw the tomb and how his body was laid.",
  "24:3": "And going in, they did not find the body of the Lord Jesus.",
  "24:4": "And it happened, as they were puzzled in their mind about this, behold, two men stood by them in shining clothing.",
  "24:5": "And as they were afraid and bowed their faces toward the ground, they said to them: Why do you seek the living among the dead?",
  "24:6": "He is not here, but is risen. Remember how he spoke to you when he was still in Galilee,",
  "24:7": "Saying: The Son of man must be handed over into the hands of sinful men and be crucified and on the third day rise again.",
  "24:9": "And going back from the tomb, they told all these things to the eleven and to all the rest.",
  "24:10": "And it was Mary Magdalene and Joanna and Mary the mother of James and the other women who were with them who told these things to the apostles.",
  "24:11": "And these words seemed to them like nonsense: and they did not believe them.",
  "24:12": "But Peter rose up and ran to the tomb and, stooping down, he saw the linen cloths lying by themselves: and he went away wondering within himself at what had happened.",
  "24:13": "And behold, two of them went that same day to a town named Emmaus, which was sixty furlongs from Jerusalem.",
  "24:14": "And they talked together about all these things which had happened.",
  "24:15": "And it happened that while they were talking and reasoning with each other, Jesus himself also drew near and went with them.",
  "24:16": "But their eyes were held, so that they did not recognize him.",
  "24:17": "And he said to them: What are these things that you are discussing with one another as you walk and are sad?",
  "24:18": "And one of them, whose name was Cleophas, answered and said to him: Are you the only stranger in Jerusalem who has not known the things that have happened there in these days?",
  "24:19": "And he said to them: What things? And they said: About Jesus of Nazareth, who was a prophet, mighty in deed and word before God and all the people,",
  "24:20": "And how our chief priests and rulers handed him over to be condemned to death and crucified him.",
  "24:21": "But we were hoping that it was he who would redeem Israel. And now besides all this, today is the third day since these things happened.",
  "24:22": "Yes, and certain women of our company also astonished us, who were at the tomb before it was light,",
  "24:23": "And not finding his body, came, saying that they had also seen a vision of angels, who say that he is alive.",
  "24:24": "And some of our people went to the tomb and found it just as the women had said: but him they did not find.",
  "24:25": "Then he said to them: O foolish and slow of heart to believe in all the things which the prophets have spoken!",
  "24:26": "Ought not the Christ to have suffered these things and so to enter into his glory?",
  "24:27": "And beginning with Moses and all the prophets, he explained to them in all the scriptures the things that concerned him.",
  "24:28": "And they drew near to the town where they were going: and he acted as though he would go farther.",
  "24:29": "But they urged him, saying: Stay with us, because it is toward evening and the day is now far spent. And he went in with them.",
  "24:30": "And it happened, while he was at table with them, that he took bread and blessed and broke it and gave it to them.",
  "24:31": "And their eyes were opened: and they recognized him. And he vanished out of their sight.",
  "24:32": "And they said to one another: Was not our heart burning within us while he spoke to us on the way and opened to us the scriptures?",
  "24:33": "And rising up that same hour, they went back to Jerusalem: and they found the eleven gathered together, and those who were with them,",
  "24:35": "And they told what had happened on the way, and how they knew him in the breaking of bread.",
  "24:36": "Now while they were speaking of these things, Jesus stood in the midst of them and said to them: Peace be to you. It is I: fear not.",
  "24:37": "But they were troubled and frightened and thought that they saw a spirit.",
  "24:39": "See my hands and feet, that it is I myself. Touch me, and see: for a spirit does not have flesh and bones, as you see me have.",
  "24:41": "But while they still did not believe and were wondering for joy, he said: Do you have anything here to eat?",
  "24:42": "And they offered him a piece of broiled fish and a honeycomb.",
  "24:43": "And when he had eaten before them, he took what remained and gave it to them.",
  "24:44": "And he said to them: These are the words which I spoke to you while I was still with you, that all things must be fulfilled which are written about me in the law of Moses and in the prophets and in the psalms.",
  "24:46": "And he said to them: Thus it is written, and thus it was necessary for the Christ to suffer and to rise again from the dead on the third day:",
  "24:47": "And that penance and forgiveness of sins should be preached in his name to all nations, beginning at Jerusalem.",
  "24:49": "And I send the promise of my Father upon you: but stay in the city until you are clothed with power from on high.",
  "24:51": "And it happened, while he blessed them, that he departed from them and was carried up to heaven.",
  "24:52": "And they, adoring him, went back to Jerusalem with great joy.",
};
